WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

01:32.790 --> 01:34.819
[birds chirping]

01:46.574 --> 01:48.602
[banging in distance]

01:51.237 --> 01:53.277
[banging continues]

02:30.147 --> 02:32.613
[lock clicks]
[keys jingling]

02:35.420 --> 02:37.352
[Duane] Jade, I need you
to start on the bathrooms.

02:37.554 --> 02:40.552
Joslyn, can you please
take out all the eggs, batter,

02:40.754 --> 02:43.587
patties and McMuffins
out of the freezer, okay?

02:43.756 --> 02:45.463
I'll help you
once I turn everything on.

02:45.632 --> 02:47.193
[sets down keys]

02:47.395 --> 02:48.465
[singsongy]
Good morning, team.

02:48.634 --> 02:50.227
[women scream]

02:50.429 --> 02:51.370
[Jeffrey]
No, no, no.

02:51.539 --> 02:52.861
Don't be scared.

02:53.064 --> 02:54.638
You just do what I say,
no one gets hurt, okay?

02:54.807 --> 02:56.199
[gasps]
No, no, look.

02:56.401 --> 02:57.676
Pointing it down.

02:57.845 --> 02:59.508
Okay, now,
I'm gonna say a polite

02:59.676 --> 03:02.204
and cheerful "Good morning,"
and then you guys say it back.

03:02.406 --> 03:03.648
Good morning.

03:03.817 --> 03:07.410
No... Duane, after I say it.

03:07.612 --> 03:09.180
That's how that works. Okay?

03:09.349 --> 03:11.050
Now, good morning, team.

03:11.219 --> 03:12.720
[all]
Good morning.

03:12.889 --> 03:14.619
Yes. Perfect.

03:14.788 --> 03:16.993
I say what to do
and you guys just do it. Okay.

03:17.162 --> 03:19.363
I want you to get
your coats back on.

03:21.031 --> 03:22.931
Duane, grab your coat.

03:23.133 --> 03:25.633
[Duane] Huh?
Grab your coat.

03:26.498 --> 03:27.998
I don't have one, sir.

03:29.539 --> 03:32.376
You don't have a coat?
How do you not have a coat?

03:33.613 --> 03:34.708
I just forgot.

03:34.877 --> 03:36.445
[sighs]

03:36.647 --> 03:38.844
Well, you're just gonna
have to be a little cold today.

03:39.543 --> 03:40.879
All right, let's go.

03:42.547 --> 03:44.522
After you. Ladies first.

03:44.691 --> 03:45.823
Now, listen to me.

03:45.992 --> 03:48.092
You guys aren't
gonna die in here.

03:48.261 --> 03:49.487
Soon as I'm out of here,
I'm gonna call the cops

03:49.656 --> 03:50.925
and they're gonna
let you guys out.

03:51.127 --> 03:52.726
Probably get the day off.

03:54.261 --> 03:56.063
No, don't, don't.

03:56.232 --> 03:57.269
Do not look at me like that.

03:59.398 --> 04:01.097
Duane, stop it.

04:01.907 --> 04:03.440
'Cause this is your fault.

04:04.204 --> 04:05.070
It's cold.

04:05.239 --> 04:06.674
Are you serious?

04:07.679 --> 04:09.347
[sighs]

04:09.516 --> 04:11.013
Dang it.

04:11.181 --> 04:12.278
I don't know what kind of jerk

04:12.480 --> 04:13.716
doesn't bring his own coat
to work.

04:13.885 --> 04:16.380
Okay? Happy now?

04:16.549 --> 04:17.586
[Duane]
My ears are cold.

04:18.850 --> 04:20.582
[Jeffrey]
<i>This is the part of the story</i>

04:20.751 --> 04:22.126
<i>where I hope you're wondering</i>

04:22.295 --> 04:24.961
<i>how a nice guy like me</i>
<i>ends up becoming a criminal.</i>

04:25.130 --> 04:26.397
[Scheimreif over speaker]
<i>Hello?</i>

04:27.426 --> 04:28.762
<i> This thing on?</i>

04:30.031 --> 04:31.468
<i>Hello?</i>

04:32.530 --> 04:33.730
[Jeffrey]
Shit!

04:33.899 --> 04:35.538
[Scheimreif over speaker]
<i>Come on, Duane.</i>

04:36.539 --> 04:38.337
Good morning.
Uh, welcome to McDonald's.

04:38.539 --> 04:40.276
I'm gonna put you on
a brief hold.

04:40.445 --> 04:42.281
[Scheimreif over speaker]
<i>What the hell, Duane?</i>

04:43.282 --> 04:44.844
[Jeffrey]
<i> I can't blame my parents.</i>

04:46.281 --> 04:47.781
<i> I had a good childhood.</i>

04:48.982 --> 04:52.253
<i> I was just never good</i>
<i> at school or behaving.</i>

04:52.422 --> 04:54.092
<i> But I was good</i>
<i> at certain things</i>

04:54.261 --> 04:57.120
<i> that were really valuable</i>
<i> to the military.</i>

04:57.963 --> 04:59.790
<i> But after my discharge,</i>

04:59.959 --> 05:02.992
<i> I didn't know where I fit</i>
<i> or what to do</i>

05:03.194 --> 05:06.461
<i>or how to give my kids</i>
<i>the things that other kids had.</i>

05:06.630 --> 05:11.605
<i> So I made some bad choices</i>
<i> that took away</i>
<i> some other choices.</i>

05:11.774 --> 05:15.013
<i> And those bad choices</i>
<i> all started two years ago</i>

05:15.215 --> 05:16.980
<i> at my daughter's</i>
<i> sixth birthday party.</i>

05:17.149 --> 05:18.678
[happy chatter]
[dog barking]

05:18.880 --> 05:20.819
[Jeffrey] All right,
you got to make a big ol' wish.

05:20.988 --> 05:23.322
[kids chattering]
[girl squeals]

05:24.452 --> 05:26.287
One more.
[scattered clapping]

05:26.456 --> 05:28.352
Did you make a wish?
What'd you wish for?

05:28.521 --> 05:30.952
[Becky] A bike.
Bike?

05:31.121 --> 05:32.226
I don't know if a bike
is exactly gonna fit

05:32.428 --> 05:35.125
into this box, but...
rip it open.

05:39.467 --> 05:41.629
[kids chattering excitedly]

05:41.798 --> 05:44.068
I'm gonna race ya. Yeah.

05:45.746 --> 05:47.511
[chatter quiets]

05:49.475 --> 05:50.745
What do you think?

05:51.779 --> 05:53.809
It's cool, right?
It's my old Erector Set.

05:53.978 --> 05:56.216
[baby babbling]
Let's open it up.

05:56.385 --> 05:58.714
There's 200 pieces in here.

05:58.883 --> 06:00.455
[pieces clattering]
[boy] No!

06:00.624 --> 06:02.684
I mean, you got engines,
you got gears, pulleys,

06:02.852 --> 06:04.395
wheels, lights, switches.

06:04.597 --> 06:06.892
We can make almost anything
that we want with this thing.

06:07.061 --> 06:10.197
Look, anything that you can
dream, we can make it, okay?

06:10.366 --> 06:12.329
Me and you. What do you say?

06:12.498 --> 06:13.871
[kid clears throat]

06:14.040 --> 06:16.069
Can you make a bike
with it?

06:16.271 --> 06:17.532
[noisemaker blows]

06:17.701 --> 06:19.235
[stammers] Yeah.

06:19.404 --> 06:20.742
Yeah.

06:21.907 --> 06:23.346
[Steve]
<i>I can't believe the dude I knew</i>

06:23.515 --> 06:26.110
<i> from the 82nd</i>
<i> can't even afford a bike.</i>

06:27.143 --> 06:28.587
Well, tell me
how you're doing so well.

06:28.789 --> 06:30.178
Well, let me see.

06:30.347 --> 06:32.184
Just this week, I got
two Japanese dudes passports.

06:32.353 --> 06:34.090
That's 5K a pop.

06:34.259 --> 06:35.850
Five grand
for fake passports?

06:36.019 --> 06:37.389
No, for real passports.
Man...

06:37.557 --> 06:38.622
Can I help you with that?

06:38.824 --> 06:40.227
Hell motherfucking no,
you can't.

06:40.396 --> 06:41.689
You can't help me with shit.

06:41.858 --> 06:43.133
[laughs] You crazy, man?

06:43.335 --> 06:44.868
You ain't helping me do
a goddamn thing.

06:45.037 --> 06:46.469
I don't need your help.

06:46.672 --> 06:48.663
Plus, we already know
that doing things the right way

06:48.832 --> 06:50.434
is not your superpower.

06:50.603 --> 06:52.605
Whatever. That's...

06:52.807 --> 06:54.439
Okay, then tell me
what my superpower is, then?

06:54.608 --> 06:56.112
Enlighten me, Buddha.
Mm.

06:56.314 --> 06:58.543
What's the flow rate
on that hose?

06:58.711 --> 07:01.084
12 gallons per minute.
Mm-hmm.

07:01.253 --> 07:03.081
How many houses is
on this street?

07:04.087 --> 07:05.254
Twenty-eight.

07:05.423 --> 07:06.887
And out of those,
how many got chimneys?

07:07.056 --> 07:08.724
Garages?

07:08.893 --> 07:10.889
How many of 'em use a heat pump
instead of a traditional AC?

07:11.058 --> 07:12.921
You want me
to sell HVAC systems
or something? Just...

07:13.090 --> 07:14.525
No, no, man,
I'm trying to make a point.

07:14.694 --> 07:16.226
Then make the point,
please.

07:16.902 --> 07:18.096
Observation.

07:18.936 --> 07:19.970
Details.

07:20.172 --> 07:21.404
You see shit
people don't see.

07:21.572 --> 07:24.600
You got like a little
X-ray vision going on.

07:24.769 --> 07:27.803
What, you think they dropped
you off in Central America
'cause you a good shot?

07:28.005 --> 07:30.379
Is that what you think?
No. No...

07:30.548 --> 07:33.314
No, they dropped you
because of what you see.

07:33.483 --> 07:34.976
Shit, if I had
a brain like yours,

07:35.178 --> 07:37.454
I'd be running
the whole goddamn world.

07:37.623 --> 07:40.250
You know, you the smartest
dumb nigga I ever known.

07:40.828 --> 07:42.060
That shit crazy.

07:42.229 --> 07:43.687
You can stop filling up
that pool now.

07:43.889 --> 07:44.996
Ain't nobody gonna
get in there.

07:45.165 --> 07:48.190
That shit cold as hell.
[laughs]

07:48.392 --> 07:49.896
[Jeffrey]<i> So, Mama</i>
<i> is probably gonna want to know</i>

07:50.065 --> 07:52.132
how the party was, and,
yeah, I think we did our best.

07:52.301 --> 07:53.732
What do you think?

07:53.901 --> 07:56.808
Maybe we don't mention
the pool. [chuckles]

07:56.977 --> 07:58.141
[entry bell jingling]

07:58.310 --> 08:00.139
It's the trying that counts,
right?

08:00.308 --> 08:01.678
[Becky] Mommy!

08:05.416 --> 08:06.982
Hi, birthday girl.
[Jeffrey sighs]

08:07.151 --> 08:08.844
How was your party?

08:09.046 --> 08:10.882
[Becky]
Everybody did their best.

08:11.084 --> 08:13.021
[Talena] Oh. Are you ready
for your other party?

08:13.223 --> 08:14.251
[car door closes]

08:15.024 --> 08:16.287
Hi.

08:16.455 --> 08:17.959
[chuckles]

08:18.128 --> 08:19.328
How are you?

08:19.497 --> 08:21.031
Hey, can I talk to you
for a second?

08:21.233 --> 08:22.530
Real-real quick, real quick.

08:22.699 --> 08:24.467
I know the last few months
haven't been easy,

08:24.636 --> 08:26.698
and we don't have the things
that we actually need,

08:26.867 --> 08:29.099
and that's my fault
and I own that.

08:29.268 --> 08:32.176
Okay? I do, but I-I think
I have it figured out now.

08:32.345 --> 08:33.607
I just got to use
my superpower and

08:33.776 --> 08:35.847
put my brain on what I want.
Your superpower?

08:36.016 --> 08:37.582
Your superpower?
Yes.

08:39.148 --> 08:40.711
[scoffs]

08:40.913 --> 08:42.582
I can't do this, Jeff.
Look-- No.

08:42.785 --> 08:43.878
I'm done.
Come on,
please don't do this.

08:44.047 --> 08:45.524
Goodbye.
[car door closes]

08:48.027 --> 08:49.485
[engine starts]

08:49.653 --> 08:50.995
[sighs]

08:51.163 --> 08:52.488
All right, banana head.

08:52.657 --> 08:54.192
Say goodbye.

08:58.863 --> 09:00.869
[Becky]
Love you!

09:10.482 --> 09:13.211
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait!

09:18.625 --> 09:20.658
[Jeffrey]
<i> I didn't blame her</i>
<i> for laughing at me.</i>

09:22.327 --> 09:24.123
<i> For thinking I was a joke.</i>

09:25.391 --> 09:28.927
<i> But there were things</i>
<i> that she didn't know about me.</i>

09:29.096 --> 09:31.636
<i>Things that weren't so funny.</i>
[ladder clattering]

09:33.538 --> 09:35.834
<i> Steve knew</i>
<i> what I was capable of.</i>

09:36.003 --> 09:38.533
<i>I do see things</i>
<i>that other people don't see.</i>

09:39.779 --> 09:43.876
<i> Like right now, I see that kid</i>
<i> climbing up that ladder,</i>

09:44.044 --> 09:45.750
<i> and I know that</i>
<i> under that flimsy roof</i>

09:45.918 --> 09:49.421
<i> is a machine that turns ground</i>
<i> beef and potatoes into money.</i>

09:49.590 --> 09:52.182
[entry bell jingles]
<i> With the same dining room,</i>

09:52.351 --> 09:55.625
<i>the same deep fryers</i>
<i>with blinking red timer lights,</i>

09:55.794 --> 09:59.455
<i> the same shake machine</i>
<i> with the same two flavors</i>

09:59.657 --> 10:02.462
<i> and the same safe full of</i>
<i> weekend corporate burger money</i>

10:02.631 --> 10:04.864
<i> that no one was gonna miss.</i>

10:05.033 --> 10:07.900
<i> They empty that safe</i>
<i> at the exact same time</i>

10:08.069 --> 10:11.470
<i> on Monday morning</i>
<i> at every single McDonald's.</i>

10:11.672 --> 10:13.040
Hi. Welcome to McDonald's.

10:13.905 --> 10:15.273
Do you know what you want?

10:15.441 --> 10:16.681
Huh?

10:17.744 --> 10:18.808
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

10:18.977 --> 10:21.445
Um, yeah, I figured it out.

10:21.614 --> 10:22.654
Thank you.

10:23.654 --> 10:25.348
[Jeffrey]
<i> There are over 10,000</i>

10:25.550 --> 10:27.923
<i> almost identical McDonald's</i>
<i> across the United States.</i>

10:29.089 --> 10:31.061
<i> Question was:</i>
<i> How many do you need to rob</i>

10:31.230 --> 10:32.795
<i> to get a real house,</i>

10:32.964 --> 10:36.162
<i> buy your kids nice things</i>
<i> and win your family back?</i>

10:37.195 --> 10:40.804
<i> Turns out,</i>
<i> the answer is 45.</i>

10:44.303 --> 10:46.741
[reporter over TV]
<i>The Roofman has struck again,</i>

10:46.910 --> 10:49.811
<i>cutting a hole through the roof</i>
<i>of this McDonald's</i>

10:49.980 --> 10:52.946
<i> at the corner of Madison</i>
<i>and Jewell in Fayetteville.</i>

10:53.115 --> 10:56.147
<i>As you can imagine, this was</i>
<i>a terrifying experience.</i>

10:56.316 --> 10:58.649
[Duane over TV]<i> He came in,</i>
<i>threw us in the freezer</i>

10:58.818 --> 11:00.158
<i>and gave me his coat.</i>

11:00.326 --> 11:02.326
<i> He gave you his coat?</i>
<i> Yes.</i>

11:02.495 --> 11:04.294
<i>Uh, yeah,</i>
<i>he didn't want me to be cold.</i>

11:04.463 --> 11:05.959
<i> He was actually</i>
<i> really nice.</i>

11:06.128 --> 11:07.927
[reporter]<i> Police believe</i>
<i> this is the same suspect</i>

11:08.096 --> 11:10.396
<i> who has been terrorizing</i>
<i> our local community</i>

11:10.599 --> 11:12.730
<i> with 45 incidents...</i>

11:12.932 --> 11:14.602
Mm.
<i> ...this past year alone.</i>

11:14.771 --> 11:16.130
<i> We have a sketch</i>
<i> of the Roofman.</i>

11:16.299 --> 11:18.974
<i> He is always</i>
<i> wearing a mask.</i>

11:19.142 --> 11:22.511
<i> He's described</i>
<i> as six-foot-two</i>
<i> with an athletic build.</i>

11:22.680 --> 11:24.382
What?
<i> The Roofman has also struck</i>

11:24.584 --> 11:26.216
<i> Burger King,</i>
<i> Kentucky Fried Chicken...</i>

11:26.385 --> 11:28.643
Nice TV you got here, Jeff.

11:28.811 --> 11:29.979
Big.

11:30.148 --> 11:31.816
How you afford
something like that?

11:31.985 --> 11:33.291
We got 15 hungry kids
out there

11:33.460 --> 11:34.523
that are
losing their minds
for cake.

11:34.692 --> 11:36.154
We got to go.
[TV volume increases]

11:36.323 --> 11:37.459
[reporter]<i> ...all of</i>
<i> these brazen incidents...</i>

11:37.628 --> 11:38.956
We got to go.
Hold on, hold on.

11:39.125 --> 11:40.531
We got to go
right now.
Let me see...

11:40.700 --> 11:42.193
If she doesn't
get her presents
right now...

11:42.362 --> 11:43.697
I want to know what's going on
with the damn suspect.

11:43.866 --> 11:44.896
...she's gonna
lose her mind.
Can I see?

11:45.065 --> 11:47.035
All right.
Why you turning it off?

11:47.203 --> 11:48.203
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait.
Don't, don't, don't, d--

11:48.372 --> 11:50.072
[groans]
Come on.

11:50.240 --> 11:51.667
Let's go.

11:51.836 --> 11:53.311
Goddamn, man.

11:53.480 --> 11:55.179
[mariachi band playing
lively music]

11:55.347 --> 11:57.375
[playing "Happy Birthday"]

12:07.188 --> 12:09.885
[band and guests]
♪<i> Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

12:10.054 --> 12:11.522
♪<i> Happy birthday</i> ♪

12:11.691 --> 12:12.955
♪<i> To you</i> ♪

12:13.157 --> 12:16.091
♪<i> Happy birthday, bandida</i> ♪

12:16.260 --> 12:19.327
♪<i> Happy birthday to you</i> ♪
You.

12:19.496 --> 12:21.300
[song continues
with lyrics in Spanish]

12:31.075 --> 12:32.446
[whoops]
[song ends]

12:32.648 --> 12:35.116
[cheering]
[whistling]

12:35.318 --> 12:36.613
Let's go!

12:36.781 --> 12:37.816
All right.

12:38.018 --> 12:40.220
Big breath, big wish.
Here we go.

12:40.853 --> 12:43.421
[cheering loudly]

12:46.129 --> 12:47.898
All right, we're gonna do
this one first this year.

12:49.369 --> 12:50.527
Big things
in little boxes.

12:52.096 --> 12:53.434
[Becky]
What is this?

12:53.603 --> 12:55.230
A garage door opener?

12:55.399 --> 12:58.137
Why'd you give me
a garage door opener?

12:58.339 --> 12:59.939
I don't know.
I just couldn't think
of anywhere else

13:00.108 --> 13:02.439
to put, uh,
the saber-toothed tiger,
so...

13:02.608 --> 13:05.381
I don't know. I couldn't put it
in the kitchen, could I?

13:05.550 --> 13:07.309
[whispering]
So, where is it?

13:07.478 --> 13:10.352
[band playing "El Fuereño"]
[cheering]

13:10.554 --> 13:12.989
[band continues playing]

13:15.125 --> 13:17.324
You're the best daddy
in the whole entire world!

13:17.492 --> 13:18.460
[laughing]

13:18.628 --> 13:19.889
Now, go ahead, get on it.

13:20.058 --> 13:21.890
[vehicles approaching]

13:22.059 --> 13:23.532
[Becky]
I love it.

13:23.734 --> 13:25.531
[tires screech]
[siren chirps]

13:25.734 --> 13:26.766
[bicycle bell jingles]

13:26.935 --> 13:28.840
[indistinct
police radio chatter]

13:30.475 --> 13:31.673
How you guys doing?

13:31.842 --> 13:34.472
We're looking
for Jeffrey Manchester.

13:35.239 --> 13:36.678
This about the registration?

13:36.881 --> 13:38.507
Yeah, I got it
right in here.
One second.

13:38.676 --> 13:40.478
["El Fuereño" continues
with lyrics in Spanish]

13:40.647 --> 13:41.547
Stop.

13:41.749 --> 13:43.518
You're under arrest!

13:43.720 --> 13:46.121
[Steve]
Whoa! Hey, hey, hey.

13:48.094 --> 13:49.322
[grunts]

13:51.154 --> 13:53.590
[officers shouting]

13:57.937 --> 13:59.937
["El Fuereño" continues
with lyrics in Spanish]

14:09.678 --> 14:11.707
[siren wailing]

14:19.890 --> 14:21.453
[officer]
Freeze! You're under arrest!

14:22.460 --> 14:24.028
[officers shouting]

14:24.196 --> 14:26.062
[grunting]

14:58.055 --> 14:59.354
[song ends]

14:59.523 --> 15:02.098
[judge]
Mr. Manchester, please rise.

15:04.232 --> 15:06.938
The State has proved
beyond the defined burden

15:07.107 --> 15:10.535
that you committed
the crime of robbery
with a dangerous weapon.

15:11.535 --> 15:13.073
I'd like to take in
consideration

15:13.242 --> 15:15.747
your service to this country
in the armed forces

15:15.916 --> 15:18.873
and the impact of your children
losing a father.

15:20.445 --> 15:22.282
<i> Now, I know</i>
<i> you got everyone fooled</i>

15:22.451 --> 15:25.723
<i> thinking you're a nice guy,</i>
<i> but I know you're a menace.</i>

15:25.892 --> 15:27.953
Although you're only
being tried for one robbery,

15:28.121 --> 15:29.658
we know you've done many more.

15:29.861 --> 15:31.454
And so the prosecution
has requested

15:31.656 --> 15:34.290
that I issue a single count
of felony kidnapping

15:34.493 --> 15:36.658
for each victim
you locked in the freezer.

15:36.860 --> 15:40.428
Let the record state that
on the 4th of February, 2004,

15:40.597 --> 15:42.770
you're hereby sentenced
to 180 months

15:42.938 --> 15:45.169
for each of the three victims,

15:45.371 --> 15:48.207
for a total of 540 months
or 45 years

15:48.376 --> 15:50.949
in the North Carolina
Department of Corrections.

15:51.981 --> 15:54.816
Mr. Sheriff,
he is in your custody.

15:55.018 --> 15:57.115
[gavel bangs]
This concludes this case.

15:57.284 --> 16:00.090
[gallery murmuring]
[lawyer whispering]

16:03.693 --> 16:05.656
[indistinct chatter]

16:16.675 --> 16:17.932
[cell door rattles, clanks]

16:20.138 --> 16:21.976
[phone line ringing]

16:22.145 --> 16:23.445
[line clicks]
[Becky over phone]<i> Hi, Daddy.</i>

16:23.614 --> 16:25.648
<i>I really missed you.</i>

16:25.817 --> 16:28.449
Miss you, too.
I miss you a lot.

16:28.618 --> 16:30.945
<i> Hey, did you get the letter</i>
<i> that I drew</i>
<i> the big ol' house on it?</i>

16:31.113 --> 16:32.681
No.

16:32.850 --> 16:33.953
<i> Well, maybe</i>
<i> it hasn't arrived.</i>
<i> Ask Mama.</i>

16:34.122 --> 16:35.791
<i>Mom says</i>
<i>she'll save the letters.</i>

16:35.960 --> 16:37.991
<i>When I'm old enough,</i>
<i>I can read them.</i>

16:38.160 --> 16:40.060
No, no. That is not...
that is not right.

16:40.262 --> 16:42.193
These letters are for,
they're for right now.

16:42.396 --> 16:43.996
[Talena] Tell him
we're cutting the cord.

16:44.165 --> 16:46.165
They said
we have to cut the cord.

16:46.334 --> 16:47.867
[Jeffrey]
<i>No, we're not cutting the cord.</i>

16:48.035 --> 16:49.500
[stammers]<i> Who said that?</i>

16:49.669 --> 16:52.871
<i>We went to a meeting for</i>
<i>families with dads in prison.</i>

16:53.040 --> 16:55.306
Okay, well, that's good.

16:55.475 --> 16:57.378
That's really good.
What'd they say there?

16:58.444 --> 17:01.981
<i>That it isn't my fault.</i>
<i>It's your fault.</i>

17:02.149 --> 17:04.847
<i>And to let you go, all the way,</i>

17:05.016 --> 17:08.718
<i> 'cause you'll never come home,</i>
<i> even if you say you will.</i>

17:08.887 --> 17:11.357
Look,
that last part is not--
that is very, very wrong.

17:11.526 --> 17:14.029
[recorded voice]
<i> You have 60 seconds remaining.</i>

17:14.198 --> 17:15.828
<i> Hey, can you put</i>
<i> your mom on for a second?</i>

17:15.997 --> 17:17.327
He wants to talk to you.

17:17.496 --> 17:19.297
No. Tell him that
you have to hang up.

17:19.466 --> 17:21.000
Gary's gonna help you
with your homework.

17:21.169 --> 17:23.037
She doesn't want
to talk to you.

17:23.206 --> 17:25.509
<i>She said I have to get off</i>
<i>and do homework.</i>

17:25.677 --> 17:27.410
<i>Gary is going to help me.</i>

17:27.579 --> 17:30.006
Gary? Who's Gary?

17:30.175 --> 17:32.210
<i> Mom's friend.</i>

17:32.379 --> 17:34.648
Huh. Mom's got
a new friend named Gary.

17:34.817 --> 17:36.348
That's-that's fun.

17:36.517 --> 17:38.054
[Talena]
It's okay, sweetheart.
You can tell him.

17:38.223 --> 17:39.050
<i>Um, okay, I'm gonna call you</i>
<i>tomorrow at the same time</i>

17:39.218 --> 17:40.182
<i> I always do, all right?</i>

17:40.351 --> 17:42.218
<i>They said no more calls.</i>

17:42.387 --> 17:43.758
No, no.
Who said that? No.

17:43.927 --> 17:45.221
[Talena]
Hang up the phone.

17:45.389 --> 17:46.588
[Gary]
It's okay, Becky.

17:46.757 --> 17:48.095
You can hang up now.
[Jeffrey]<i> Hang up?</i>

17:48.297 --> 17:49.599
Is that Gary?
Put him on the phone
right now.

17:49.801 --> 17:51.365
[Talena]
<i>Hang up. Hang up.</i>

17:51.534 --> 17:54.737
Put Gary or your mom
on the phone right now,
Becky, okay?

17:54.906 --> 17:56.530
[Becky]
<i>I have to hang up.</i>
Hey.

17:56.699 --> 17:57.972
<i> Listen to me,</i>
<i> I'm coming home.</i>

17:58.174 --> 17:59.868
<i> Tell your brothers</i>
<i> I'm coming home.</i>

18:00.037 --> 18:01.405
<i>And we don't say goodbye,</i>
<i>'cause goodbye means going away</i>

18:01.574 --> 18:02.912
and going away means
forgetting, and we're...

18:03.081 --> 18:05.347
[click, dial tone drones]
We're-- H-Hello?

18:06.319 --> 18:08.043
Hello?

18:08.212 --> 18:09.945
B... Becky?

18:24.731 --> 18:26.570
[prisoner]<i> Why is you</i>
<i> still thinking about them?</i>

18:26.738 --> 18:28.304
<i> You got to let that go.</i>

18:29.302 --> 18:30.471
Ain't no
getting out of here.

18:31.469 --> 18:33.408
Get that idea
out your head.

18:35.445 --> 18:37.573
[Jeffrey]<i> Every prisoner</i>
<i> wants the same thing:</i>

18:37.742 --> 18:39.777
<i> to get out of prison.</i>
[tools buzzing]

18:39.945 --> 18:42.309
<i> And they think</i>
<i> that the way out</i>
<i> is through a wall</i>

18:42.478 --> 18:43.644
<i> or over a fence.</i>

18:43.813 --> 18:45.948
<i> But the guards</i>
<i> got that covered.</i>

18:47.160 --> 18:50.090
<i> The way out of prison</i>
<i> is through the people.</i>

18:50.259 --> 18:52.587
<i> Prison was</i>
<i> just another building</i>

18:52.756 --> 18:55.123
<i> full of systems</i>
<i> and routines.</i>

18:55.291 --> 18:58.331
<i> Keep the routine,</i>
<i> and the guards</i>
<i> won't get suspicious.</i>

18:58.500 --> 19:01.499
<i> If you're nice enough,</i>
<i> if you're useful,</i>

19:01.668 --> 19:04.472
<i> they forget</i>
<i> you're in there</i>
<i> for a reason.</i>

19:05.472 --> 19:07.404
<i> And when they stop</i>
<i> watching you,</i>

19:07.573 --> 19:08.808
<i> you can start</i>
<i> watching them.</i>

19:08.977 --> 19:09.943
You smell that?

19:10.112 --> 19:11.815
Smells like you're leaking.

19:11.984 --> 19:13.311
How 'bout
checking it out
for me.

19:13.480 --> 19:15.846
Yes, sir.
See if you see
anything.

19:19.018 --> 19:20.521
Yeah.

19:21.453 --> 19:23.492
Doesn't look too bad
just yet.

19:23.661 --> 19:25.490
I don't know--
it'll probably get you back
to where you're going.

19:25.659 --> 19:28.625
All right.
Well, come on out of there.
All right.

19:28.793 --> 19:30.634
Yeah, you better
tell your maintenance guy.

19:30.803 --> 19:32.626
You might need a new gasket.

19:32.795 --> 19:34.033
I appreciate it, man.
Yes, sir.

19:34.202 --> 19:35.734
Have a good one.
You, too.

19:40.947 --> 19:43.346
[truck door closes]
[engine starts]

20:05.231 --> 20:07.029
[tools buzzing]

20:22.688 --> 20:24.915
[whistling a tune]

20:32.389 --> 20:33.594
[door opens]

20:55.352 --> 20:57.214
[tools buzzing]
[truck back-up alarm beeping]

20:57.383 --> 20:59.422
[truck engine rumbling]

21:13.596 --> 21:15.306
Yeah. Straight back.

21:17.502 --> 21:19.137
Two boxes.
[Jeffrey] Yep.

21:19.306 --> 21:20.477
Two benches.
Yes, sir.

21:20.645 --> 21:22.137
All right.

21:24.210 --> 21:26.248
Shut her down.

21:26.417 --> 21:28.814
She's all yours,
Mr. Cummings.
Thank you, bud.

21:30.780 --> 21:32.249
Hey, smells
like you fixed it.

21:32.418 --> 21:34.157
[chuckles] Good catch.

21:34.326 --> 21:37.020
All right, drive safe.
All right,
have a good one.

21:45.529 --> 21:47.228
[truck door closes]

21:49.302 --> 21:51.199
[engine starts]

22:18.270 --> 22:21.229
[engine idling]
[low, indistinct chatter]

22:31.608 --> 22:34.110
[chatter continues]

22:43.128 --> 22:45.792
[brakes hissing]
[engine rumbling]

23:30.208 --> 23:33.367
[tires screech]
[brakes hiss]

23:35.738 --> 23:37.712
[truck door opens]

23:37.881 --> 23:39.582
Jesus.

23:43.546 --> 23:44.950
Phew.

23:49.358 --> 23:51.385
[belt jangles]
[zipper whizzes]

23:55.129 --> 23:57.160
[sighs]

24:11.278 --> 24:13.507
[belt jangles]

24:13.710 --> 24:15.277
[zipper whizzes]

24:34.907 --> 24:36.936
[engine starts]

25:20.144 --> 25:22.179
[dog barking in distance]
[insects chirping]

25:42.305 --> 25:44.267
[Jeffrey laughing softly]

25:46.376 --> 25:47.875
[Jeffrey whispering]
Yeah.

25:48.876 --> 25:51.377
Yeah, pedal, pedal, pedal,
pedal, pedal.

25:51.545 --> 25:53.551
[Jeffrey laughing softly]

26:12.530 --> 26:13.565
[grunts]

26:13.734 --> 26:16.739
["S'Cudjo" by Zé Manel playing]

26:18.274 --> 26:20.237
[phone ringing]

26:20.406 --> 26:21.640
Hello?

26:21.842 --> 26:23.338
[Jeffrey over phone]
<i> Steve. It's me.</i>

26:23.507 --> 26:26.040
Jeff, Jeff, what the fuck
are you doing calling me, man?

26:26.209 --> 26:28.350
You all over the goddamn news
and shit.

26:28.519 --> 26:30.045
Look, I got to get
out of the country.

26:30.214 --> 26:32.113
I'm thinking, like,
Brazil or Venezuela.

26:32.282 --> 26:33.718
Somewhere with a beach
and no extradition.

26:33.887 --> 26:35.652
[Steve]
<i>God, you sound fucking crazy.</i>

26:35.854 --> 26:37.252
[stammers]
I know. I'm sorry.

26:37.421 --> 26:39.295
<i> Don't do no stupid shit</i>
<i>like go see your family.</i>

26:39.497 --> 26:41.054
<i> Hide. All right?</i>
Okay. Okay. I'll hide.

26:41.223 --> 26:42.397
<i>Don't call back</i>
<i>for another month.</i>

26:42.566 --> 26:43.894
All right,
I'm-a call you in a month.

26:44.063 --> 26:45.132
And don't call
my motherfucking phone again.

26:45.301 --> 26:47.467
You got it? A'ight.

26:47.636 --> 26:49.464
[click, dial tone drones]
Steve?

26:49.632 --> 26:50.938
St--

26:52.438 --> 26:53.776
[sighs]

27:22.966 --> 27:25.005
[cart wheels rattling]

27:33.242 --> 27:35.279
[music playing
over vehicle stereo]

27:44.286 --> 27:46.323
[light music playing
over speakers]

27:47.299 --> 27:48.696
[Mitch] You.
[girl] A lot.

27:48.865 --> 27:50.529
[Mitch]
A lot? We have-- Yep.
What do you want?

27:50.698 --> 27:52.400
[girl] A monkey.
A monkey?

27:52.602 --> 27:54.236
[kids chattering]
Wait a minute.

27:54.438 --> 27:55.702
[boy] Turtle.
[Mitch] Turtle.

27:55.904 --> 27:56.938
What--
and what do you want?
[girl] Candy.

27:57.107 --> 27:58.437
Candy?

27:58.606 --> 28:00.268
We got a lot of candy.

28:00.437 --> 28:03.541
Uh, um, sir,
we're closing here
in ten minutes.

28:03.710 --> 28:05.749
Sir?
Yeah, no problem.

28:07.516 --> 28:09.544
[toys beeping, chirping]

28:11.451 --> 28:13.119
I got you.

28:20.725 --> 28:22.766
[toy beeping]

28:25.830 --> 28:27.870
[toy phone ringing]

28:30.175 --> 28:32.803
[toy gun firing]

28:32.972 --> 28:35.009
[indistinct chatter
over speakers]

28:36.743 --> 28:38.782
[toy laser gun firing]

28:49.523 --> 28:51.355
[door creaks]

28:55.562 --> 28:57.031
[door closes]

29:07.342 --> 29:09.813
[panting]

29:22.393 --> 29:23.421
[shoes squeak on toilet]

29:23.590 --> 29:25.753
[grunting]

29:25.922 --> 29:28.661
[door opens]

29:28.863 --> 29:30.626
[indistinct
police radio chatter]

29:30.828 --> 29:32.231
[door closes]

29:37.940 --> 29:39.574
[indistinct police radio
chatter continues]

29:39.743 --> 29:40.770
[officer over radio]
<i>Zero, three, six,</i>

29:40.939 --> 29:42.772
<i>five, nine, eight, two.</i>

29:42.941 --> 29:45.079
[footsteps approaching]

29:46.949 --> 29:49.116
[indistinct police radio
chatter continues]

29:52.153 --> 29:54.749
[officer] Bathroom's clear.
[door opens, closes]

29:54.917 --> 29:56.354
[exhales]

29:58.420 --> 29:59.658
[Mitch over speakers]
<i> Attention,</i>

29:59.826 --> 30:01.224
<i> Toys "R" Us customers.</i>

30:01.393 --> 30:04.765
<i> Our store will be closing</i>
<i> in five minutes.</i>

30:04.934 --> 30:07.296
<i> So, if you are not a toy</i>
<i> or an employee,</i>

30:07.465 --> 30:10.265
<i> please bring your purchases</i>
<i> up to the front.</i>

30:10.434 --> 30:12.467
<i> Whether you are a kid</i>
<i> or a parent</i>

30:12.636 --> 30:15.268
<i> or an uncle or a friend</i>
<i> making a dream come true,</i>

30:15.437 --> 30:17.911
<i> it is time</i>
<i> to make your choices</i>

30:18.079 --> 30:20.780
<i> and meet us</i>
<i> at the register up front.</i>

30:20.949 --> 30:24.214
<i>If you can't decide tonight,</i>
<i>don't worry.</i>

30:24.416 --> 30:26.381
<i> We promise you</i>
<i> we will be here tomorrow,</i>

30:26.584 --> 30:29.519
just as long as you promise us
to never grow up.

30:38.666 --> 30:40.068
[exhales quietly]

30:49.511 --> 30:52.147
[clattering]

30:52.316 --> 30:54.676
[toy squeaks]

31:16.408 --> 31:18.469
[shoes squeaking softly]

31:25.009 --> 31:26.609
[doors creaking]

31:44.666 --> 31:46.101
[unzips backpack]

32:27.344 --> 32:28.569
[exhales]

32:28.738 --> 32:30.508
[news anchor]
<i> Jeffrey Manchester, also known</i>

32:30.710 --> 32:33.507
<i>as the Roofman, escaped</i>
<i>from Brown Creek Prison</i>
<i>earlier today.</i>

32:33.709 --> 32:35.884
<i> Tonight, he's still</i>
<i>out there somewhere.</i>

32:36.052 --> 32:38.054
[reporter]<i> Authorities</i>
<i>discovered Manchester,</i>

32:38.222 --> 32:42.249
<i> who was serving 45 years for</i>
<i>armed robbery and kidnapping,</i>

32:42.418 --> 32:44.121
<i>was missing this afternoon...</i>

32:44.290 --> 32:46.695
Ha.
<i>...during a routine head count.</i>

32:46.898 --> 32:48.862
<i>Correction officers</i>
<i>do not know the method</i>

32:49.064 --> 32:50.357
<i>or exact time</i>
<i>of Manchester's escape...</i>

32:50.560 --> 32:51.968
They still don't know
how I got out.

32:52.137 --> 32:54.434
<i> ...but believe he may still be</i>
<i> in the Charlotte area.</i>

32:54.603 --> 32:56.564
No, no, no. I'm-I'm long gone.
[Scheimreif]
<i> We believe he fled</i>

32:56.733 --> 32:59.875
<i>sometime between 12:00 and 4:00</i>
<i>this afternoon.</i>

33:00.077 --> 33:02.444
<i>He's a very smart individual.</i>
<i>Super intelligent.</i>

33:02.613 --> 33:04.041
<i>Probably genius level.</i>

33:04.243 --> 33:05.979
<i>But he's also</i>
<i>an absolute idiot.</i>

33:06.148 --> 33:09.179
<i>We believe that the suspect</i>
<i>could be armed.</i>

33:09.381 --> 33:11.918
<i>And he has a history</i>
<i>of violent behavior.</i>

33:12.087 --> 33:13.613
What?
[reporter]<i> Police are asking</i>

33:13.782 --> 33:16.354
<i>if you see someone</i>
<i>who looks like Manchester,</i>

33:16.523 --> 33:20.129
<i> please call authorities</i>
<i>and do not confront him.</i>

33:33.170 --> 33:35.804
[birds chirping]

33:37.305 --> 33:39.346
[busy chatter]

33:44.984 --> 33:47.024
[chair creaking]

33:54.532 --> 33:56.825
[Jeffrey exhales]

33:57.863 --> 33:59.630
[chuckles]

34:07.576 --> 34:08.837
Okay.

34:10.007 --> 34:11.312
All right.

34:11.481 --> 34:13.040
Yeah.

34:13.208 --> 34:14.342
[chuckles]

34:14.511 --> 34:16.186
Password:
one, two, three, four,

34:16.354 --> 34:18.352
five, six.

34:20.985 --> 34:22.587
[mutters]

34:30.534 --> 34:31.794
Whoa. Yeah.

34:42.673 --> 34:44.175
[Jeffrey]<i> Most guys,</i>
<i> when they escape,</i>

34:44.344 --> 34:46.609
<i> get caught</i>
<i> in the first few hours.</i>

34:46.811 --> 34:49.443
<i> They go as far as they can</i>
<i> as fast as they can.</i>

34:49.612 --> 34:52.155
[knocks]
<i> And that never works.</i>

34:54.120 --> 34:55.422
<i> The trick is to stop.</i>

34:56.718 --> 34:59.155
<i> Find a place</i>
<i> no one will look.</i>

34:59.357 --> 35:02.396
["Free" by Ultra Naté playing]

35:12.410 --> 35:13.902
[mutters]

35:23.148 --> 35:25.980
[Jeffrey]<i> Sometimes,</i>
<i> the best hiding places</i>
<i> are in plain sight.</i>

35:27.423 --> 35:30.626
<i> A place where people are</i>
<i> too preoccupied to see you.</i>

35:30.795 --> 35:33.363
<i> So I kept quiet as a mouse.</i>

35:33.565 --> 35:35.090
<i> But not at night.</i>

35:35.259 --> 35:37.160
<i> I owned the night.</i>

35:37.362 --> 35:40.830
♪<i> Where did we go wrong?</i> ♪

35:41.896 --> 35:43.639
[reporter]
<i> The manhunt for the Roofman</i>

35:43.807 --> 35:45.238
<i> enters its third day.</i>

35:45.407 --> 35:47.469
[Jeffrey]<i> People</i>
<i> have short attention spans.</i>

35:47.638 --> 35:50.247
<i> After a while,</i>
<i> they get bored.</i>

35:50.415 --> 35:52.512
<i> I figured I had to</i>
<i> be quiet for about a month,</i>
<i> give or take.</i>

35:52.681 --> 35:55.115
[reporter]
<i> Still no leads from police</i>
<i> on the whereabouts</i>

35:55.284 --> 35:58.217
<i> of escaped convict</i>
<i> Jeffrey Manchester,</i>

35:58.419 --> 36:00.484
<i> as the manhunt enters</i>
<i> its eighth day.</i>

36:00.653 --> 36:02.824
[Jeffrey]<i> One time,</i>
<i> when I was in the 82nd,</i>

36:02.993 --> 36:04.354
<i> I spent 30 days</i>
<i> in the woods</i>

36:04.523 --> 36:07.095
<i> surviving off of</i>
<i> rainwater and grubs.</i>

36:07.263 --> 36:09.857
<i> Your body doesn't need much</i>
<i> to keep going.</i>

36:10.059 --> 36:13.531
<i> It's your brain</i>
<i> that you have to</i>
<i> take care of.</i>

36:13.733 --> 36:15.431
<i> If you can make your brain</i>
<i> imagine a better place,</i>

36:15.600 --> 36:17.599
<i> it can get you</i>
<i> through anything.</i>

36:17.768 --> 36:20.676
<i> Just pick any place</i>
<i> but where you are.</i>

36:20.845 --> 36:22.471
<i> Like a beach on an ocean.</i>

36:22.640 --> 36:24.374
<i> A place where</i>
<i> your kids can visit</i>

36:24.543 --> 36:26.341
<i> after everyone else</i>
<i> forgets you.</i>

36:26.510 --> 36:27.750
[reporter]
<i> Nearly two weeks</i>

36:27.953 --> 36:29.246
<i> since Jeffrey Manchester</i>
<i> escaped</i>

36:29.448 --> 36:30.819
<i> from Brown Creek Penitentiary.</i>

36:30.988 --> 36:33.485
<i> Police have set up</i>
<i> roadblocks,</i>

36:33.654 --> 36:36.485
<i> concerned Manchester</i>
<i> may still be in the area.</i>

36:36.654 --> 36:37.992
<i> Sergeant,</i>
<i> I'm with Channel 6 News.</i>

36:38.161 --> 36:39.786
<i> Jeffrey Manchester's</i>
<i> still missing.</i>

36:39.955 --> 36:41.358
<i> Do you think he could be</i>
<i> in Charlotte?</i>

36:41.527 --> 36:43.065
[Scheimreif]
<i> He might've kept moving,</i>

36:43.267 --> 36:44.693
<i> but we're not gonna give up</i>
<i> on the possibility</i>

36:44.861 --> 36:46.867
<i> that he still might be</i>
<i> hiding out here</i>

36:47.035 --> 36:48.531
<i> in Mecklenburg County.</i>

36:48.700 --> 36:51.164
<i>And when he tries to run,</i>
<i>we'll be ready.</i>

36:51.839 --> 36:53.100
Good luck.

36:54.142 --> 36:55.736
♪<i> Never trust another</i> ♪

36:55.905 --> 36:57.442
♪<i> 'Cause they're all out</i>
<i> to getcha</i> ♪

36:57.644 --> 37:00.010
♪<i> We have to live</i>
<i> in this world together</i> ♪

37:00.179 --> 37:01.877
♪<i> 'Gether</i> ♪

37:02.046 --> 37:05.115
♪<i> If we open up our heart,</i>
<i> love can finally start</i> ♪

37:05.317 --> 37:07.281
♪<i> Come on and try</i> ♪

37:07.484 --> 37:08.724
♪<i> Now's the time</i> ♪

37:08.893 --> 37:11.651
♪<i> 'Cause you're free</i> ♪

37:11.820 --> 37:14.830
♪<i> To do what you want to do</i> ♪

37:14.999 --> 37:19.427
♪<i> You got to live your life</i> ♪

37:19.629 --> 37:22.097
♪<i> Do what you want to do</i> ♪

37:22.300 --> 37:24.530
[shoes squeak]

37:24.699 --> 37:26.600
♪<i> Do what you want</i> ♪

37:26.768 --> 37:28.402
♪<i> Do what you want to do</i> ♪

37:28.571 --> 37:30.210
♪<i> Do what you want</i> ♪

37:30.379 --> 37:32.876
♪<i> Do what you want to do ♪</i>
[song fades]

37:51.866 --> 37:53.127
[grunts]

37:56.703 --> 37:57.797
[Leigh over headphones]
<i> One quick question.</i>

37:57.966 --> 37:59.838
[Mitch over headphones]
<i> Uh, yeah.</i>

38:00.040 --> 38:02.171
[Leigh]<i> Okay. I just</i>
<i> wanted to talk to you</i>
<i> about my hours.</i>

38:02.373 --> 38:03.406
[chuckles]
<i> Um...</i>

38:03.574 --> 38:04.945
<i>I need every other weekend off.</i>

38:05.113 --> 38:06.244
[Mitch]
<i> I'm confused.</i>

38:06.412 --> 38:08.511
<i> First you ask me</i>
<i> for a job,</i>

38:08.714 --> 38:10.918
<i> and now you're asking me</i>
<i> for time off.</i>

38:11.086 --> 38:12.414
[Leigh]
Well, you know,

38:12.583 --> 38:14.053
I'm a team player...
Yeah.

38:14.222 --> 38:16.425
...but, um, I'm also a mom.

38:16.594 --> 38:17.891
I know.

38:18.060 --> 38:19.795
Okay. Well...
I do.

38:19.964 --> 38:22.393
Uh...
You-you reminded me.

38:22.562 --> 38:25.466
I got a divorce
six months ago, so...

38:25.635 --> 38:27.969
<i> it's really hard for me to</i>
<i>balance everything right now</i>

38:28.138 --> 38:30.701
<i>with work and my girls</i>
<i>and my ex.</i>

38:30.903 --> 38:33.000
Oh, come on. [mutters]
<i> The custody situation is:</i>

38:33.169 --> 38:36.706
They have, you know,
one weekend him,
one weekend me.

38:36.909 --> 38:39.615
I don't want to bore you
with my personal problems.

38:39.784 --> 38:43.813
Good, good. 'Cause I
don't want to be bored
by your personal problems.

38:43.982 --> 38:46.947
If this is
a Toys "R" Us problem,
then I'm interested.

38:47.115 --> 38:49.955
But personal problems
belong on personal time.

38:50.124 --> 38:51.688
[clicks tongue]

38:51.890 --> 38:54.524
Thank you, Leigh.
Got to get back to payroll.

38:54.727 --> 38:56.192
Work, work, work, work,
work, work, work.

38:56.394 --> 38:57.461
<i> Good to see you.</i>

38:57.630 --> 38:58.698
[Jeffrey] What a dick.
<i>Thanks, Mitch.</i>

38:58.867 --> 39:00.035
<i> Okay.</i>

39:00.204 --> 39:01.464
[door closes]
[Mitch]<i> Unbelievable.</i>

39:01.633 --> 39:03.535
Yeah, you're
an unbelievable dick.

39:03.704 --> 39:05.565
<i> I know you're a mom.</i>
<i> You mentioned it before.</i>

39:05.767 --> 39:08.203
<i> Mom card. Unbelievable.</i>

39:08.371 --> 39:09.676
[stammers]

39:10.707 --> 39:12.239
[Jeffrey]
Dollar sign, U,

39:12.441 --> 39:14.113
C, C, E,

39:14.281 --> 39:17.184
dollar sign, dollar sign.

39:17.353 --> 39:19.281
That's the dumbest password
I've ever...

39:19.450 --> 39:20.523
I've ever heard of.

39:20.691 --> 39:22.359
"$ucce$$."

39:26.029 --> 39:27.025
[computer chimes]
Heh.

39:27.194 --> 39:28.994
[mouse clicking]

39:29.163 --> 39:30.724
[clicking tongue]

39:30.893 --> 39:32.501
[goofy voice]
We found Leigh.

39:33.528 --> 39:35.328
Saturday.

39:35.497 --> 39:37.065
Goodbye.

39:37.234 --> 39:40.502
Boop, boop, boop, boop, boop,
boop, boop, boop, boop, boop.

39:40.670 --> 39:41.769
[pops lips, clicks tongue]

39:41.971 --> 39:44.238
You have the day off now.
[pops lips]

39:44.440 --> 39:45.974
Voilà.

39:46.143 --> 39:47.680
[news theme plays]
[announcer]
<i> The news starts now.</i>

39:47.849 --> 39:49.983
[news anchor]<i> More than</i>
<i> 30,000 folks are expected</i>

39:50.152 --> 39:51.650
<i> to crowd into town.</i>

39:51.819 --> 39:53.156
[reporter]<i> ...came up with</i>
<i> the idea "Babe Wash."</i>

39:53.325 --> 39:56.149
<i> And the bikinis do</i>
<i> bring in the business.</i>

39:56.318 --> 39:57.654
[reporter 2]<i> The biggest</i>
<i> celebrations of the Fourth</i>

39:57.823 --> 40:00.093
<i> take place in the skies</i>
<i> right behind me.</i>

40:00.262 --> 40:01.291
[Jeffrey]
<i> People get bored</i>

40:01.493 --> 40:03.533
<i> with last week's news.</i>

40:03.701 --> 40:06.931
<i> Pretty soon,</i>
<i> they can't even remember</i>
<i> why they know your face.</i>

40:08.198 --> 40:11.100
<i>Even cops lose interest</i>
<i>unless you really piss 'em off.</i>

40:13.773 --> 40:15.670
<i> Everybody forgets you</i>
<i> eventually.</i>

40:15.839 --> 40:18.509
[fireworks whistling
and popping]

40:18.678 --> 40:20.912
<i> Except people</i>
<i> who really love you.</i>

40:27.553 --> 40:29.525
[fireworks continue popping]

40:37.595 --> 40:40.801
<i> I couldn't get to</i>
<i> the people who love me now</i>
<i> without hurting them.</i>

40:40.969 --> 40:44.400
<i> The only place</i>
<i> I might ever see them again</i>
<i> was somewhere else</i>

40:44.569 --> 40:47.269
<i> and some other time.</i>

40:47.437 --> 40:50.438
<i> The first step was</i>
<i> getting out of here...</i>
[pliers click]

40:50.607 --> 40:52.746
<i> ...to get there.</i>

41:12.761 --> 41:14.801
[phone line ringing]

41:16.435 --> 41:17.431
[Michelle]
<i> Hello?</i>

41:17.599 --> 41:19.274
Hi. Um...

41:19.443 --> 41:21.571
Wh-- Is, uh--
May I, may I speak to Steve?

41:21.740 --> 41:23.769
Please?
Sorry, who is this?

41:23.938 --> 41:25.347
<i> Oh, this is a friend.</i>

41:25.550 --> 41:27.843
<i>Well, I mean, this is...</i>
<i>Oliver. His, uh, his cousin.</i>

41:28.045 --> 41:30.152
[chuckles]<i> I was--</i>
<i> I'm doing this little...</i>

41:30.321 --> 41:31.750
little cross-country trip,
and, uh,

41:31.919 --> 41:33.688
he was, he was expecting me.
I was supposed to visit.

41:33.857 --> 41:35.289
Mm. Mm.

41:35.458 --> 41:37.291
He didn't say anything
about a visit.

41:37.460 --> 41:39.052
And I didn't know
he had a cousin.

41:39.254 --> 41:41.291
He must have forgot
to mention it, I guess.

41:41.460 --> 41:42.560
Um... [stammers]

41:42.762 --> 41:43.998
Who am I sp--
who am I speaking with?

41:44.167 --> 41:45.330
<i>Oh, I'm his girlfriend.</i>

41:45.499 --> 41:47.028
What is this about, though?

41:47.197 --> 41:49.872
'Cause I'm in the middle
of something, so, uh...

41:50.074 --> 41:51.798
<i> His girl-- okay, great.</i>

41:51.967 --> 41:53.666
<i> Could I talk to Steve now?</i>

41:53.835 --> 41:55.168
<i> He isn't here.</i>

41:55.336 --> 41:57.142
Okay, well,
should I call back
in, like, a...

41:57.311 --> 41:58.810
like, an hour or so?

41:58.979 --> 42:02.118
Uh, well, he's not gonna be
back until December 1st.

42:02.287 --> 42:04.182
<i> Where does anyone go</i>
<i> till December?</i>

42:04.351 --> 42:05.888
<i>He's in Afghanistan.</i>

42:06.057 --> 42:07.752
He's not in Afghanistan.

42:07.955 --> 42:09.323
<i> We got back two years ago</i>
<i> from Afghanistan.</i>

42:09.492 --> 42:12.020
Well, he took
a six-month contract.

42:12.188 --> 42:15.565
Um, but he asked me
to take messages for him.

42:16.697 --> 42:17.900
<i>Is there something</i>
<i> that you want me</i>

42:18.069 --> 42:19.767
<i>to tell him if he calls?</i>

42:22.467 --> 42:23.801
Yeah, uh...

42:23.970 --> 42:26.672
tell him that, uh,
Cousin Oliver is gonna stay

42:26.840 --> 42:28.906
with relatives in the area
until he's back

42:29.108 --> 42:30.914
<i> on December 1st</i>
<i> for a really</i>
<i> important meeting.</i>

42:31.116 --> 42:32.347
Okay, I will tell him that.

42:32.516 --> 42:34.640
And, uh, I will see you then,
too, I guess.

42:34.809 --> 42:36.051
Cousin Oliver.

42:36.220 --> 42:38.115
[laughs]<i> Bye.</i>
[line clicks]

42:43.159 --> 42:44.958
[dial tone drones]

42:45.160 --> 42:48.030
[line ringing]

42:48.198 --> 42:49.764
[Becky over phone]
<i>Hello?</i>

42:50.828 --> 42:52.692
Stop tickling me. Just a sec.

42:52.861 --> 42:54.564
Hello? [giggles]

42:54.732 --> 42:56.705
[giggling]
<i>Gary is crazy.</i>

42:56.874 --> 42:58.669
<i>Gary!</i>

42:58.838 --> 43:01.407
[Gary laughing]
<i>Who is it? Hello?</i>

43:01.576 --> 43:03.438
[Gary laughing]
[giggling] Gary!

43:03.640 --> 43:04.939
Hello?
Gary.

43:05.141 --> 43:07.377
<i> Who is this?</i>
[Becky continues giggling]

43:07.546 --> 43:09.243
<i>Jeff, is this you?</i>

43:09.412 --> 43:12.882
<i> If you call here again,</i>
<i>I'm gonna call the cops.</i>

43:13.051 --> 43:14.956
<i> Do you hear me?</i>
[Jeffrey crying softly]

43:15.125 --> 43:16.953
<i>We've moved on.</i>

43:17.122 --> 43:19.786
<i>And you need</i>
<i>to move on, too.</i>
[Becky chattering]

43:19.955 --> 43:21.559
<i>Don't call here anymore.</i>

43:21.728 --> 43:23.765
[line clicks]
[dial tone drones]

43:27.038 --> 43:29.232
[panting softly]

43:39.378 --> 43:40.815
[sighs]

44:06.406 --> 44:08.403
[clattering]

44:10.742 --> 44:12.979
[clattering continues]

44:21.918 --> 44:24.058
[Elmo toy laughing]

44:24.261 --> 44:25.454
[Elmo]
<i>That tickles.</i>

44:25.622 --> 44:27.763
[laughing]

44:36.097 --> 44:38.834
<i>Oh, boy, that tickles.</i>

44:39.003 --> 44:41.568
[distorted]
<i>Elmo wants to play.</i>

44:41.770 --> 44:44.175
[laughing]

44:47.342 --> 44:49.175
<i> Let's play.</i>
[overlapping chatter]

44:49.344 --> 44:50.878
[Elmo 2]
<i> Oh, boy, that tickles.</i>

44:51.046 --> 44:52.851
[Elmo 3]
<i> Elmo love you.</i>

44:53.019 --> 44:56.357
<i>Elmo wants to play.</i>
<i>You're Elmo's sweetheart.</i>

44:56.525 --> 44:58.553
<i> That tickles.</i>
<i> Let's play.</i>

44:58.756 --> 44:59.821
<i> Elmo love you.</i>

44:59.989 --> 45:01.791
<i> Oh, boy, that tickles.</i>

45:01.960 --> 45:03.322
[distorted,
overlapping chatter]

45:03.491 --> 45:05.791
<i> Let's play.</i>
[Elmo singing "The ABC Song"]

45:05.960 --> 45:07.168
<i>Elmo love you.</i>

45:07.337 --> 45:09.233
<i>Elmo loves his ABCs...</i>

45:09.435 --> 45:11.499
[humming]

45:13.010 --> 45:14.200
[sputters]

45:14.369 --> 45:16.109
Hey, Leigh.
[Mitch]
Otee-Otee-Otis.

45:16.312 --> 45:17.837
[murmurs]
Hey.

45:18.006 --> 45:19.447
[Otis]
Hey, Mitch.

45:19.649 --> 45:21.214
You're just the man
I want to see.

45:21.383 --> 45:22.609
[time clock clicks]

45:23.581 --> 45:24.787
Cool.

45:24.989 --> 45:26.683
You, uh...

45:26.852 --> 45:28.649
you like Peanut M&Ms, right?

45:28.818 --> 45:29.924
Yeah.
Yeah?

45:30.126 --> 45:31.387
Yeah.

45:32.830 --> 45:34.387
[Mitch over headphones]
<i> 'Cause we're missing a lot</i>

45:34.555 --> 45:36.722
<i> of Peanut M&Ms.</i>
<i> You have any idea why?</i>

45:36.891 --> 45:38.600
<i> No.</i>

45:38.802 --> 45:40.501
[Mitch]
<i>What's wrong?</i>
[Otis]<i> Nothing's wrong.</i>

45:40.670 --> 45:42.168
[Mitch]
<i>Seem nervous.</i>
[Otis]<i> I'm not.</i>

45:42.337 --> 45:43.437
[Leigh]
<i>No.</i>

45:43.606 --> 45:45.769
[Mitch]
No?
No. Not happening.

45:45.938 --> 45:47.535
You can't talk to him
like that.

45:47.704 --> 45:50.245
Okay. You know, we are missing
half a dozen boxes out there.

45:50.414 --> 45:51.710
And I just thought-- boop--

45:51.879 --> 45:53.915
they got to be hiding
somewhere-- boop.

45:57.112 --> 45:58.851
[Leigh]
<i>I am so sorry.</i>

45:59.020 --> 46:01.553
[Mitch]
<i>Oh, God.</i>
<i>He cannot talk to you that way.</i>

46:01.722 --> 46:03.086
[Mitch]
<i>I'm the bad guy now.</i>

46:03.255 --> 46:04.921
[Leigh]<i> Hey. You got to</i>
<i>stick up for yourself.</i>

46:05.090 --> 46:06.459
<i>Okay? Or he's just</i>
<i> gonna get worse.</i>

46:06.661 --> 46:09.257
I'm not big
on conflict, so...

46:09.425 --> 46:11.429
Yeah.
Okay, well,
we'll-we'll work on that.

46:11.598 --> 46:13.066
[Otis]
<i> Cool.</i>

46:21.936 --> 46:26.107
[Leigh]<i> Listen, Mitch,</i>
<i> you really hurt</i>
<i> Otis's feelings,</i>

46:26.276 --> 46:28.010
<i> and I think</i>
<i> you should apologize.</i>

46:28.212 --> 46:29.979
[Mitch]<i> I'm sorry.</i>
[Jeffrey mumbles]

46:30.181 --> 46:31.487
[Leigh]
<i> Well, that's a good start.</i>

46:31.689 --> 46:32.916
[Mitch chuckles]<i> Okay.</i>
[Leigh]<i> You know,</i>

46:33.085 --> 46:34.649
<i> people respect kindness</i>
<i> in a leader.</i>

46:34.852 --> 46:35.918
[Mitch]
<i> Mm.</i>

46:36.086 --> 46:37.491
[Leigh]
<i> W-With that in mind,</i>

46:37.694 --> 46:39.787
<i>I wanted to invite you</i>
<i>to my church.</i>

46:39.956 --> 46:41.424
<i>Crossroads Church.</i>

46:43.062 --> 46:44.892
It's, uh, just across
the interstate.

46:45.061 --> 46:46.429
Uh...
Have you been?

46:47.469 --> 46:48.935
Not very churchy.

46:49.104 --> 46:50.966
Okay, well, I'm in charge
of the toy drive there,

46:51.135 --> 46:52.374
and it got me thinking,
here I am,

46:52.577 --> 46:54.709
working in a toy store
of all places,

46:54.912 --> 46:58.680
and you haven't even donated
one toy to my toy drive.

46:58.849 --> 47:01.846
Well, we sell toys here.
We don't give 'em away.

47:02.048 --> 47:03.485
Okay. What about
all those returned toys?

47:03.654 --> 47:05.679
Perfectly good ones
that we can't sell.

47:06.919 --> 47:08.918
We run a business here,
Leigh.

47:09.087 --> 47:11.822
Okay.
Well, you can still come.

47:11.991 --> 47:13.629
You know,
all people are welcome.

47:13.797 --> 47:16.126
<i>Even if they're mean</i>
<i>or aren't quite ready yet.</i>

47:16.295 --> 47:19.060
<i>So you can come, bring</i>
<i>a big bag of toys, or not.</i>

47:19.263 --> 47:20.726
[Jeffrey chuckles]
<i>You'll be welcome.</i>

47:20.928 --> 47:24.032
<i> But bring the toys and you</i>
<i>could be a good guy for once.</i>

47:24.201 --> 47:26.634
<i>Don't you want to be</i>
<i>a good guy?</i>

47:27.677 --> 47:29.243
<i> Come on, Mitch! Be a good guy!</i>

47:29.446 --> 47:30.880
[Mitch]
<i> Okay.</i>

48:29.569 --> 48:30.567
[sighs]

48:30.735 --> 48:32.405
[mutters]

48:32.574 --> 48:34.240
Is that garbage?

48:34.409 --> 48:36.439
Uh...

48:36.641 --> 48:39.414
Huh?
Do you want me to put that
in the garbage for you?

48:39.582 --> 48:40.944
It's just toys for the...

48:41.146 --> 48:42.681
Uh, I heard
there was a toy drive.

48:42.850 --> 48:44.686
Well, it's right
this way.

48:44.855 --> 48:46.619
It's o-- I'll just
leave 'em here. It's okay.

48:46.821 --> 48:47.919
[chuckles]
I'm not gonna walk

48:48.088 --> 48:50.421
all the way down there
in these heels.

48:55.466 --> 48:56.890
It's very nice
of you.

48:57.059 --> 48:58.397
Here you go.

48:58.565 --> 48:59.799
Thank you.

48:59.968 --> 49:01.735
[laughs]
Oh, it's too heavy
for me.

49:01.904 --> 49:03.462
[chuckles]
Got to bring it on
in there.

49:03.631 --> 49:04.737
Come on, I'll show you
where the toys go.

49:04.906 --> 49:05.969
Where do you want me
to put 'em?

49:06.171 --> 49:07.739
You can bring 'em
right in here.

49:07.908 --> 49:09.908
Service
is about to begin.

49:10.077 --> 49:12.110
[light gospel music
playing inside]

49:12.279 --> 49:13.974
[Pastor Ron]
Anyone that feels
alone out there...

49:14.176 --> 49:15.417
[music continues]

49:15.585 --> 49:16.911
...just come on down here.

49:17.080 --> 49:18.111
[speaking quietly]

49:18.280 --> 49:19.618
'Cause you belong here.

49:19.787 --> 49:21.252
We're all sinners here,

49:21.421 --> 49:23.685
which is why I ask my wife
sometimes to sing this tune.

49:24.793 --> 49:26.919
♪<i> In times of despair</i> ♪

49:28.562 --> 49:31.633
♪<i> I think about</i>
<i> The good things</i>
<i> That you've done</i> ♪

49:31.802 --> 49:34.329
[congregation whooping
and murmuring]

49:34.498 --> 49:38.671
♪<i> Ooh, and though</i>
<i> You're not there</i> ♪

49:38.873 --> 49:40.768
♪<i> I sometimes ask myself</i> ♪

49:40.936 --> 49:43.408
[Pastor Ron]
♪<i> Is anyone?</i> ♪
[Eileen] ♪<i> Is anyone? ♪</i>

49:45.109 --> 49:46.749
♪<i> Yeah</i> ♪
♪<i> Oh</i> ♪

49:46.918 --> 49:50.452
[choir joins in]
♪<i> It's so hard being human</i> ♪

49:50.621 --> 49:51.946
♪<i> With all the troubles</i> ♪

49:52.115 --> 49:56.491
♪<i> In sight</i> ♪

49:56.660 --> 49:58.451
♪<i> But somehow I know</i> ♪

49:58.620 --> 50:01.995
♪<i> I know, I know,</i>
<i> I know, I know</i> ♪

50:02.163 --> 50:05.960
♪<i> Everything's gonna</i>
<i> Work out all right</i> ♪

50:06.129 --> 50:07.535
♪<i> Hey, yeah</i> ♪

50:07.704 --> 50:12.008
♪<i> But somehow I know</i> ♪

50:13.306 --> 50:17.810
♪<i> Everything's gonna</i>
<i> Work out all right</i> ♪

50:17.979 --> 50:22.975
♪<i> Hey, but somehow I know</i> ♪

50:24.284 --> 50:28.987
♪<i> Everything's gonna</i>
<i> Work out all right</i> ♪

50:29.156 --> 50:32.493
[song ends]
[cheering and applauding]

50:32.662 --> 50:33.689
[Eileen]
Hallelujah.

50:37.325 --> 50:39.898
[lively chatter]

50:40.100 --> 50:42.701
Wow. Somebody is
very hungry, huh?

50:42.870 --> 50:44.530
Big appetite there, huh?

50:44.699 --> 50:46.171
[mouth full] Sorry.
[laughs] Please.

50:46.340 --> 50:47.907
I haven't had food this good
in so long. [chuckles]

50:48.110 --> 50:50.575
No, that's great.
Big food for a big guy.

50:50.777 --> 50:51.877
Yeah.
Yeah.

50:52.046 --> 50:53.542
Now, you can't sneak
out of here

50:53.711 --> 50:55.440
without saying hello
to the pastor and his wife.

50:55.642 --> 50:56.618
No.
It's against the rules.

50:56.820 --> 50:57.780
No, I would never.
I would never.

50:57.982 --> 50:58.912
I'm Eileen.

51:00.021 --> 51:01.890
John. Z-- uh, Zorin.
John Zorin.

51:02.059 --> 51:03.882
Yeah, I haven't seen you
around the area before.

51:04.051 --> 51:05.860
I noticed you,
obviously, in the,
in the-the row there.

51:06.029 --> 51:07.362
Where are you from?
You new to the area?

51:07.531 --> 51:09.229
Yeah, uh, I'm-I'm...

51:09.398 --> 51:13.434
[sighs] I'm just new
to this place
and, really, everything.

51:13.637 --> 51:15.770
You know, it's, um...

51:15.972 --> 51:17.729
All of this is
really just, you know...

51:17.898 --> 51:19.234
Every-Everything here
is just new for me.

51:19.403 --> 51:21.169
I'm-I'm down
from New York City.

51:21.338 --> 51:22.535
That's
a walking man's town,

51:22.704 --> 51:24.242
I mean, if ever
I've been-been to one.

51:24.411 --> 51:26.038
That is
a walking man's town.
That is correct.

51:26.206 --> 51:28.951
I bet you go through a lot
of pair of sneakers, don't you?

51:29.120 --> 51:30.409
[laughs] Everyone does.
Right? Do you go through...

51:30.578 --> 51:32.116
Yeah, yeah.
Oh, my. You've--

51:32.285 --> 51:34.151
You got very small feet
for a big guy.

51:34.354 --> 51:36.088
No, I actually have
large feet. It's just,

51:36.257 --> 51:37.551
I put on the wrong shoes,
and I don't know,

51:37.720 --> 51:39.962
I think these are, like,
nines in women's.

51:40.131 --> 51:42.595
And I'm sorry, I would never
wear sneakers to church.

51:42.764 --> 51:44.197
I-I'm really sorry.

51:44.366 --> 51:46.363
You know, I-I would like
to introduce you to someone.

51:46.531 --> 51:48.867
I'd like to introduce you
to Leigh Wainscott.

51:49.036 --> 51:50.565
She runs the toy drive here,

51:50.733 --> 51:53.104
and I heard you gave
such a generous donation.

51:53.273 --> 51:54.869
I know she'd like
to thank you for it.

51:55.038 --> 51:57.145
You know, she looks a bit busy
over there, actually, Eileen.

51:57.314 --> 51:59.139
She's having a serious
conversation with her daughter.

51:59.308 --> 52:01.282
[chatter fades]

52:06.147 --> 52:07.316
Now?

52:07.485 --> 52:08.814
[Pastor Ron]
Yeah.
[Eileen] We can.

52:08.983 --> 52:10.120
Yeah. Okay.
You made such
a great donation.

52:10.289 --> 52:11.320
Okay. Yeah, sure.
Yeah. Hey, hey.

52:11.489 --> 52:13.593
Okay, great.
Uh, Leigh. Hey, Leigh.

52:13.762 --> 52:15.093
Leigh. Hey, Leigh.

52:15.262 --> 52:17.091
Come, come say hi
to our mystery man.

52:17.260 --> 52:18.157
Okay.
Come on.

52:18.359 --> 52:19.260
Yeah.
Yeah.

52:19.429 --> 52:20.999
This is our all-star Leigh.

52:21.201 --> 52:22.298
She is the backbone
of everything

52:22.467 --> 52:24.102
that is good going on
in this church.

52:24.271 --> 52:26.102
She does the outreach,
does the meals,

52:26.271 --> 52:27.802
does the toy drive,
she...

52:27.971 --> 52:30.269
I really don't know how
she does it all, but she does.

52:30.438 --> 52:32.944
And this is John...

52:33.113 --> 52:35.350
Zorin? Zorin from New York.

52:35.519 --> 52:36.952
Oh, New York.

52:37.121 --> 52:39.517
That's far from here.
Yeah, a little bit, yeah.

52:39.686 --> 52:42.889
[Eileen] So, John-- he made
a very generous toy donation.

52:43.091 --> 52:45.486
Oh, that's so kind
of you. We...

52:45.655 --> 52:47.328
Couldn't have come
at a better time.

52:47.496 --> 52:50.765
No, I-I mean, um,
I really like Christmas
and-and birthdays,

52:50.933 --> 52:52.096
uh, and just
gift-giving time.

52:52.264 --> 52:53.662
[laughs]
I mean, I don't know.

52:53.831 --> 52:55.971
[stammers]
I just love kids.
You have kids, John?

52:56.139 --> 52:59.304
Well...
You have a family,
or are you single?

52:59.472 --> 53:01.138
I'm, uh, just officially
divorced, that's all.

53:01.307 --> 53:02.404
[Pastor Ron]
Oh, I'm sorry, John.

53:02.606 --> 53:03.644
Not-not all marriages
work out, right?

53:03.813 --> 53:05.540
That's-- that is true.

53:05.709 --> 53:07.375
But to answer your question,
I do have kids.

53:07.544 --> 53:09.016
I have two little
monster boys,

53:09.185 --> 53:11.214
and I got a little girl
that is my best pal.

53:11.382 --> 53:12.878
That's sweet.
And, um... Yeah.

53:13.046 --> 53:14.551
But they're in New York,
and I'm here working.

53:14.720 --> 53:16.716
And what-what-what do you--
what do you do for work?

53:16.918 --> 53:19.355
Well, I... [sighs]
I-I work for the government,

53:19.524 --> 53:22.026
um, but I can't exactly
talk about it.

53:22.194 --> 53:23.897
It's, uh, it's classified

53:24.100 --> 53:25.859
and all that silliness.
[Eileen] Oh.

53:26.028 --> 53:28.702
Well, John Zorin from New York,
our New York spy.

53:28.871 --> 53:29.969
No! No, no.
[laughter]

53:30.138 --> 53:31.065
Definitely not that.
I like that.

53:31.234 --> 53:33.001
Okay, okay.

53:33.170 --> 53:35.371
Well, can I ask you,
can we count on you
to join us next Sunday?

53:35.540 --> 53:36.878
Yeah.
Well, and also
this Wednesday.

53:37.047 --> 53:38.680
Oh. Wow. Yeah.
What's-what's Wednesday?

53:38.849 --> 53:40.377
Uh, I run a singles dinner,

53:40.546 --> 53:43.111
and this week's gonna be
at a Red Lobster.

53:43.314 --> 53:44.845
I love a Red Lobster.

53:45.014 --> 53:46.313
I mean,
not just the seafood.
Those cheese biscuits...

53:46.482 --> 53:47.514
Mm-hmm.
I mean, yeah.

53:47.683 --> 53:48.590
I-I mean,
are you gonna be there?

53:48.792 --> 53:51.183
[Eileen]
Hmm. Leigh?

53:51.351 --> 53:53.920
You think you're gonna join us
for our first single dinner?

53:54.122 --> 53:56.996
Well, I never thought of myself
as being a single,

53:57.165 --> 53:59.758
but, sure, yeah,
I-I'll-I'll go.

53:59.960 --> 54:01.703
[Eileen] Okay.
Yeah, I'll-I'll be there.

54:01.872 --> 54:03.269
Count me in.
[Eileen] Okay.

54:03.437 --> 54:05.273
[Kami] Good to see you.
Thank you so much.

54:05.442 --> 54:06.466
Thank you for joining us today.
Really appreciate it.

54:06.668 --> 54:07.974
[Jeffrey]
<i> I liked being John</i>

54:08.177 --> 54:09.538
<i> better than I liked</i>
<i> being Jeff.</i>

54:09.707 --> 54:11.071
See you on Wednesday.
Wednesday. Yes, ma'am.

54:12.112 --> 54:13.713
<i> John was a good guy.</i>

54:13.882 --> 54:15.708
<i> People liked him.</i>

54:15.877 --> 54:17.749
<i> Leigh seemed to</i>
<i> like him, too.</i>

54:17.918 --> 54:20.852
<i> But there was no way</i>
<i> a girl like her</i>
<i> was gonna really fall</i>

54:21.021 --> 54:24.216
<i> for a guy</i>
<i> in women's running shoes</i>
<i> and a Spider-Man T-shirt.</i>

54:24.385 --> 54:25.720
[groans]

54:25.889 --> 54:27.930
<i> Also, I really needed</i>
<i> to see a dentist.</i>

54:28.099 --> 54:30.596
<i> Living on candy is</i>
<i> hard on your teeth.</i>

54:35.365 --> 54:36.998
[entry bell jingles]

54:38.106 --> 54:39.564
Good afternoon.
How are you?

54:39.733 --> 54:41.009
Good, sir.
How are you?

54:41.211 --> 54:44.009
[bag unzips]
See what you give me
for these.

54:44.211 --> 54:46.515
Uh, how about
ten apiece? 300.

54:46.717 --> 54:47.983
Yeah, I'll go 300.

54:48.152 --> 54:49.210
Okay, let's do that.
Yeah, deal. Yes, sir.

54:49.379 --> 54:51.815
M.O.D. on number 29.

54:53.214 --> 54:55.887
14 cavities. That's a lot
of cavities for an adult.

54:56.056 --> 54:57.087
Yeah, I'm sorry.

54:57.256 --> 54:58.489
I just have a bit--

54:58.691 --> 55:00.118
naturally, I guess,
a bit of a sweet tooth,

55:00.287 --> 55:02.294
and I've had access
to a lot of really good candy.

55:02.463 --> 55:03.557
Just haven't been able to...
Open your mouth

55:03.725 --> 55:05.159
wide, please.
...s-stop. Okay.

55:05.327 --> 55:07.600
[whirring]

55:10.570 --> 55:12.034
[laughter, lively chatter]
[pop music playing]

55:12.236 --> 55:13.771
Look at those.

55:19.817 --> 55:21.115
Oh, wow. [chuckles]

55:21.284 --> 55:23.818
[Kami chuckles]
[excited chatter, clapping]

55:23.987 --> 55:25.684
[Jeffrey]
Hello. [chuckles]

55:26.748 --> 55:28.853
Hello, ladies.
[women] Hi!

55:29.055 --> 55:30.122
Hi.
Hi.

55:30.291 --> 55:31.793
How is everyone?
[chuckles]
Good.

55:31.962 --> 55:33.324
Oh, okay.
[women chuckling]

55:33.493 --> 55:34.993
I thought this was
a singles brunch,

55:35.162 --> 55:36.457
not a supermodel brunch.

55:36.625 --> 55:39.025
[laughter]
Ooh. [laughs]

55:39.194 --> 55:41.635
[Kami] You could always
squeeze in down here by us.

55:41.803 --> 55:42.905
[laughter]

55:43.107 --> 55:45.500
Well, we wanted
to welcome you, John.

55:45.668 --> 55:47.032
[Kami] Yes.
Welcome, welcome.

55:47.201 --> 55:48.201
Am I the only guy
that's gonna be here today?

55:48.370 --> 55:49.405
[laughs]

55:49.607 --> 55:51.012
[women] Yes.
Uh-huh. Yep. You are.

55:51.181 --> 55:53.114
Turns out to be so, yes.
Right. Okay.

55:53.283 --> 55:55.041
Yes. I hope we're not
overwhelming for you.

55:55.244 --> 55:57.042
Oh, no, no, no,
I'm actually-- I-I'm
liking it very much.

55:57.244 --> 55:59.217
Okay, good.
I love having
so many new friends,

55:59.420 --> 56:01.052
especially beautiful friends.
Um...

56:01.254 --> 56:03.052
Ooh.
[woman]
Sweet one.

56:03.254 --> 56:06.825
So, John, I understand
you work for the government.
What kind of work?

56:06.994 --> 56:10.758
I-I would love
to get into those details,
but I'm undercover, so, um...

56:10.960 --> 56:12.826
[women oohing]
Oh, that sounds mysterious.

56:12.995 --> 56:15.069
No, I can promise
it's not that mysterious.

56:15.238 --> 56:17.539
It's really quite boring.
[chuckles]

56:17.707 --> 56:21.007
I never knew there was
an intelligence unit
here in Charlotte.

56:21.176 --> 56:22.701
Oh, are you law enforcement?

56:22.870 --> 56:24.338
I'm retired now,
but I was.

56:24.507 --> 56:26.208
Wow. That's amazing.

56:26.377 --> 56:27.376
[high-pitched gasp]

56:27.545 --> 56:28.675
Am I, am I, uh...
[laughter]

56:28.844 --> 56:30.017
Am I arrested?
How does this work?

56:30.186 --> 56:31.680
I don't want to
make you upset.

56:31.849 --> 56:33.154
[Kami]
You're embarrassing
everyone, Sally.

56:33.323 --> 56:35.551
He did not come here
to be interrogated.

56:35.720 --> 56:37.750
No, no, no,
I actually really like it.

56:37.919 --> 56:39.551
I feel a lot safer
with her here.

56:39.720 --> 56:41.396
Um, but-but yeah.

56:41.565 --> 56:43.559
Um, there's intelligence
just about in every major city.

56:43.728 --> 56:45.765
We just don't advertise
that much, yeah.

56:45.934 --> 56:49.798
Well, if he's undercover,
why's he at a singles dinner
at Red Lobster?

56:50.000 --> 56:52.035
[overlapping chatter]
That's a fair question.

56:52.203 --> 56:53.338
Well...

56:53.507 --> 56:55.574
That's a fair question.
I-I can...

56:55.743 --> 56:57.444
That is, that is a question
that is not classified.

56:57.646 --> 57:00.748
I am here possibly looking
for the next Ms. John Zorin.

57:00.917 --> 57:03.008
[laughter, applause]

57:03.177 --> 57:05.119
Oh, please. Oh, please.
[Jeffrey stammers]

57:05.322 --> 57:07.515
See, but there-there
is a problem, though.

57:07.684 --> 57:11.388
I'm having a bit of an issue
that there's just
too many beautiful choices here

57:11.557 --> 57:12.985
to choose from.
[excited chatter]

57:13.187 --> 57:14.790
No, I'm-I'm sorry.
I should not have said that.

57:14.959 --> 57:16.759
My mom always told me
do not compliment a woman

57:16.928 --> 57:20.233
on her beauty because
it makes her self-conscious.

57:20.402 --> 57:21.427
Um, always start
with their shoes.

57:21.595 --> 57:22.564
[laughter]

57:22.732 --> 57:24.138
Speaking of.
Hold on a second.

57:24.340 --> 57:26.300
Let me get
under this table.
[laughter]

57:26.502 --> 57:27.734
Excuse me.

57:27.903 --> 57:30.308
Got some high boots
down there.

57:30.511 --> 57:33.080
Stilettos at brunch.
All right, girl.

57:33.249 --> 57:35.643
[laughter continues]
Okay, okay.

57:35.845 --> 57:37.315
[Kami]
It is getting hot in here.

57:37.517 --> 57:39.449
[lively chatter]
No, no, no, no.

57:39.617 --> 57:41.114
[Leigh]
<i> That was really fun.</i>

57:41.283 --> 57:42.921
Look, I don't get out much,
so this was fun for me.

57:43.090 --> 57:44.619
Me neither.

57:44.788 --> 57:46.322
[chuckles]
You sure made their day.

57:46.491 --> 57:47.789
They made my day, truly.

57:47.958 --> 57:48.997
This is my car.
I mean, I've never been...

57:49.166 --> 57:50.092
This is you? Ooh, a Subaru.
Yeah.

57:50.261 --> 57:51.325
Yeah.

57:51.493 --> 57:53.168
I like it.

57:53.337 --> 57:55.504
All right,
I'm-I'm getting
my courage up.

57:55.706 --> 57:57.000
Um...

57:58.098 --> 57:59.641
I have two questions
to ask you.

57:59.810 --> 58:01.471
Two? Just two?

58:01.640 --> 58:02.935
Yeah.
All right.
Let's hear it.

58:03.104 --> 58:05.143
Drumroll. Give me
the first one. Go.

58:05.312 --> 58:07.740
Um, you're gay, right?

58:07.909 --> 58:09.784
What? I'm what?
You're gay.

58:09.953 --> 58:10.950
Gay? No.
Yeah.

58:11.119 --> 58:12.218
[laughs]
What?

58:12.421 --> 58:13.982
Are you kidding
right now?
No, I...

58:14.151 --> 58:15.785
No, I mean, look,
I don't have
anything against gays.

58:15.954 --> 58:17.985
I love gays,
but, like, I'm--
no, absolutely not.

58:18.153 --> 58:19.820
You just...
What made you think
I was gay?

58:19.989 --> 58:21.459
You just seem like
one of the girls.

58:21.628 --> 58:23.989
Or, like, you seem
to love women's shoes.

58:24.158 --> 58:25.525
No, that's not
what that was.
[laughs]

58:25.694 --> 58:26.959
All right.
Uh-uh.

58:27.128 --> 58:28.169
All right, well, that--
if that's a no,

58:28.338 --> 58:29.598
we can go straight
to question two.

58:29.767 --> 58:32.532
Okay. Uh, yeah.
I guess, hit me.

58:32.734 --> 58:33.834
[chuckles]
Um...

58:34.003 --> 58:36.612
Um, would you like
to go out with me?

58:36.780 --> 58:38.613
On a date?

58:41.246 --> 58:42.347
Okay.

58:42.516 --> 58:45.246
Wow, you're
a very forward person.

58:47.648 --> 58:49.382
I, uh...

58:51.024 --> 58:54.722
Um, yes, I would,
I would very much--
really, very much--

58:54.891 --> 58:56.426
like to go out
on a date with you.

58:56.628 --> 58:58.131
[laughs]
I don't know, yes.

58:58.300 --> 58:59.900
Yes is the answer
to that.

59:00.102 --> 59:01.234
All right.
Okay.

59:01.437 --> 59:04.166
I'm free, um,
next Saturday morning?

59:04.335 --> 59:05.503
Perfect.

59:05.672 --> 59:07.374
I'll pick you up.
Where do you live?

59:07.543 --> 59:11.336
[sputters]
I live in
a really boring, uh,

59:11.505 --> 59:14.913
government building
that's non-disclosed
to the public.

59:16.184 --> 59:17.217
How about this?

59:17.386 --> 59:20.219
Uh, let's meet
at Freedom Park.

59:20.388 --> 59:23.018
Saturday morning,
8:00 a.m.

59:23.187 --> 59:26.357
Sounds like a,
like a-- uh, well,
sounds like a date.

59:26.526 --> 59:27.522
It's a date.
So it's a date.

59:27.691 --> 59:29.154
Okay. Bye.
Okay. Bye.

59:29.323 --> 59:31.264
All right. All right. Sorry.
Hey. [laughs]

59:31.467 --> 59:33.028
You were shaking,
and I was going...

59:33.197 --> 59:34.828
But don't get...
There's a car.
[gasps] Oh, shit.

59:34.996 --> 59:36.269
[laughs] Okay.
All right. Yep.

59:36.472 --> 59:38.168
All right,
that was awkward.
Okay.

59:38.337 --> 59:39.432
See ya.
Bye!

59:54.255 --> 59:55.288
[Leigh]
It's hot.

59:55.457 --> 59:57.153
[Jeffrey]
It's hot. [grunts]

59:58.421 --> 59:59.786
Wow.

59:59.988 --> 01:00:01.719
You're in
really good shape.

01:00:01.888 --> 01:00:02.797
Thanks, girl.

01:00:02.999 --> 01:00:04.626
[both laugh]

01:00:04.828 --> 01:00:07.101
My ex, Jeffrey, he...
Yeah?

01:00:07.269 --> 01:00:09.467
What?
You said Jeffrey.

01:00:09.670 --> 01:00:12.369
Yeah. That's my ex's name--
Jeffrey.

01:00:12.538 --> 01:00:13.766
Got it, right.
Yeah.

01:00:13.935 --> 01:00:14.899
His name
was Jeffrey?

01:00:15.068 --> 01:00:16.471
Yeah. He was in...
Wow.

01:00:16.640 --> 01:00:17.846
...horrible shape.

01:00:18.048 --> 01:00:21.149
Like, we had no...

01:00:21.318 --> 01:00:22.778
No...?
It's just been
a long time.

01:00:22.947 --> 01:00:24.582
Oh, okay.
But we're nothing alike.

01:00:24.751 --> 01:00:26.613
Good to know.
Yeah, I-I like people.

01:00:26.782 --> 01:00:28.181
He didn't talk.

01:00:28.383 --> 01:00:31.783
He just read war history novels
on the toilet.

01:00:31.952 --> 01:00:32.894
[laughs]
What?

01:00:33.063 --> 01:00:34.229
Mm-hmm.
[gags]

01:00:34.398 --> 01:00:36.822
N-No, Jeffrey,
that is gross.
[laughs]

01:00:37.024 --> 01:00:39.459
Right? [laughs]
[gags]

01:00:39.628 --> 01:00:43.098
He loves his books,
but when it comes to
time for the girls

01:00:43.267 --> 01:00:46.841
or homework
or driving lessons,
just doesn't show up.

01:00:47.009 --> 01:00:48.643
Stressful.

01:00:48.812 --> 01:00:50.210
I just think you need
a little bit more fun
in your life,

01:00:50.412 --> 01:00:52.208
to be honest.
[stammers]

01:00:54.511 --> 01:00:55.684
Okay.

01:00:57.348 --> 01:01:00.546
Do you want to go
back to mine and have
some fun right now?

01:01:03.124 --> 01:01:04.187
What?

01:01:05.227 --> 01:01:07.025
Really?
Mm-hmm.

01:01:08.164 --> 01:01:09.461
Yes. Very much, yes.

01:01:09.630 --> 01:01:11.495
I would very much--
yeah, mm-hmm.

01:01:11.663 --> 01:01:13.330
Okay.
Mm-hmm. Yeah. Now?

01:01:13.499 --> 01:01:14.593
Yeah.
All right.

01:01:25.644 --> 01:01:27.408
Told you I wasn't gay.

01:01:27.610 --> 01:01:29.544
[laughing]

01:01:29.713 --> 01:01:32.347
Shut up.
[laughing]

01:01:33.380 --> 01:01:34.949
[Jeffrey]
Tell me about your daughters.

01:01:35.118 --> 01:01:37.353
[Leigh] Their names
are Dee and Lindsay.

01:01:37.521 --> 01:01:38.986
Dee's 11.

01:01:39.155 --> 01:01:41.888
She's pretty sensitive
and creative.

01:01:42.090 --> 01:01:43.995
She's like...
I don't know.

01:01:44.164 --> 01:01:47.728
She-she hasn't let me
cut her hair
since she was a baby.

01:01:47.930 --> 01:01:49.267
She's one of those kids.

01:01:49.470 --> 01:01:50.866
And then Lindsay's 16.

01:01:51.035 --> 01:01:53.405
She has a sign
on her door that says,

01:01:53.574 --> 01:01:55.203
"Emotionally unavailable."

01:01:55.372 --> 01:01:58.174
[laughs softly]
She also just
got her learner's permit

01:01:58.343 --> 01:02:00.879
but refuses to drive,
even though
she wants her freedom,

01:02:01.048 --> 01:02:03.282
so that's where we're at.
Oh, is that right? [laughs]

01:02:03.484 --> 01:02:04.915
Well, I'm a good driver.

01:02:05.117 --> 01:02:06.681
If you want me to teach her,
I-I'll happily do it.

01:02:06.850 --> 01:02:09.017
[laughs]
We just met.

01:02:09.186 --> 01:02:11.420
That's a good point.
That's a... [stammers]

01:02:11.622 --> 01:02:12.523
Yeah, I know.

01:02:12.692 --> 01:02:14.552
Um, I just love kids, so...

01:02:14.721 --> 01:02:18.193
Okay, well, maybe...
maybe you could
meet 'em sometime.

01:02:18.362 --> 01:02:22.467
You know, like, maybe
you could come over for...

01:02:22.669 --> 01:02:24.539
for pizza one weekend,
maybe?

01:02:24.707 --> 01:02:26.703
Like a pizza party?
Can we have a pizza party?

01:02:26.871 --> 01:02:28.441
Like a pizza Saturday?
[laughs]

01:02:28.610 --> 01:02:30.311
I haven't been
out of the house,

01:02:30.513 --> 01:02:32.213
let alone on a date, okay?
Okay.

01:02:32.382 --> 01:02:34.408
In a very long time.
Mm-hmm.

01:02:34.577 --> 01:02:37.845
Um, I... I don't know
if my girls are ready
for, you know,

01:02:38.014 --> 01:02:40.020
M-Mom to be dating
just yet.

01:02:40.189 --> 01:02:41.513
I get that.

01:02:41.682 --> 01:02:43.387
We can still have a pizza party
and just make it

01:02:43.556 --> 01:02:46.087
just totally normal.

01:02:46.256 --> 01:02:49.023
I'm just a friend from church,
you know,

01:02:49.192 --> 01:02:50.725
that happens to be
a government spy.

01:02:50.894 --> 01:02:52.223
[laughs]
A non-gay one.

01:02:52.392 --> 01:02:53.634
You know,
a non-gay government spy

01:02:53.802 --> 01:02:55.326
that just comes over
and wants to, you know,

01:02:55.528 --> 01:02:58.098
have pizza with you
and your daughters.

01:02:58.267 --> 01:03:00.231
You know, just make it normal.
Okay.

01:03:00.400 --> 01:03:01.933
You're-you're not normal,
John,

01:03:02.102 --> 01:03:03.001
but...
[snickers]

01:03:03.203 --> 01:03:05.775
[laughing]
I like you.

01:03:05.944 --> 01:03:08.242
You know what's not normal?
Hmm?

01:03:08.411 --> 01:03:10.713
You just look like this
all the time?
[scoffs]

01:03:10.882 --> 01:03:13.754
Looking inviting.
[laughing]

01:03:13.923 --> 01:03:16.583
[Jeffrey mumbles playfully]
[Leigh squeals, laughs]

01:03:18.591 --> 01:03:20.620
[birds chirping]

01:03:42.250 --> 01:03:43.852
[sighs]

01:04:10.104 --> 01:04:12.111
[bags rustling]

01:04:17.015 --> 01:04:19.186
[knocking on door]
[Leigh] Oh.

01:04:19.355 --> 01:04:21.154
He's here. Okay?

01:04:21.323 --> 01:04:22.684
[door opens]

01:04:22.853 --> 01:04:23.882
[Jeffrey]
Hello.

01:04:24.085 --> 01:04:25.888
Please come in.

01:04:26.056 --> 01:04:27.725
Wow, that's
a lot of food.

01:04:27.894 --> 01:04:30.727
Girls,
this is my friend John.

01:04:30.895 --> 01:04:33.331
John, these are my girls.

01:04:33.500 --> 01:04:34.896
Hey, girls.

01:04:35.065 --> 01:04:37.197
Uh, hi.
I'm-I'm John Zorin.

01:04:37.366 --> 01:04:40.337
I'm your mom's good friend
from church.

01:04:41.674 --> 01:04:43.508
You must be Dee.

01:04:43.677 --> 01:04:45.013
That's short for Delia?

01:04:45.182 --> 01:04:46.648
Yeah.
Yes.

01:04:46.816 --> 01:04:49.147
You must be Lindsay,
and that's short for...

01:04:49.316 --> 01:04:52.817
That's not short for anything
at all, actually. [laughs]

01:04:52.986 --> 01:04:54.853
Look, I've heard
so much about you guys.

01:04:55.022 --> 01:04:57.849
Uh, and one of the things
that I have heard,

01:04:58.018 --> 01:05:02.954
is that you, Dee,
happen to be a huge fan
of<i> Zelda,</i> like I am.

01:05:03.156 --> 01:05:04.089
Is that true?

01:05:04.258 --> 01:05:05.731
Yeah.
Is that right?

01:05:05.900 --> 01:05:07.265
Good, 'cause I got you
this Link doll.

01:05:07.434 --> 01:05:08.631
[laughs]

01:05:08.834 --> 01:05:10.737
And another question:

01:05:10.906 --> 01:05:13.538
[whispering]
Have you played<i> Four Swords?</i>

01:05:13.707 --> 01:05:14.906
No.
It is so amazing,

01:05:15.075 --> 01:05:16.236
and it comes with
this special controller

01:05:16.405 --> 01:05:17.235
that I'll teach you
how to use later

01:05:17.404 --> 01:05:18.878
until you can whup my butt,

01:05:19.047 --> 01:05:20.781
which you'll probably be able
to do really quickly

01:05:20.983 --> 01:05:22.115
''cause I hear you're,
like, a<i> Zelda</i> master.

01:05:22.317 --> 01:05:24.078
[laughs]

01:05:24.246 --> 01:05:25.713
Thanks.
Yes.<i> Zelda</i> worked.

01:05:25.881 --> 01:05:26.847
One down.

01:05:27.016 --> 01:05:29.119
Lindsay, for you,

01:05:29.288 --> 01:05:32.393
I have an assortment
of very angsty teenage music

01:05:32.562 --> 01:05:35.121
for your listening pleasure.

01:05:35.290 --> 01:05:37.625
[laughs]
[Leigh] Thank you?

01:05:38.367 --> 01:05:39.660
No, thank you.

01:05:40.867 --> 01:05:43.866
Nice to meet you,
John Zorin,

01:05:44.034 --> 01:05:46.766
Mom's friend from church.

01:05:51.011 --> 01:05:52.871
Where are you going?
I have homework.

01:05:53.948 --> 01:05:55.548
[sighs heavily]
[Jeffrey] It's okay.

01:05:55.716 --> 01:05:57.109
[laughs]
Maybe next time.

01:05:57.278 --> 01:05:58.376
Okay?
[Leigh groans]

01:05:58.545 --> 01:06:00.480
All right? Don't worry.
[sighs]

01:06:00.649 --> 01:06:03.521
I, uh, also happened
to have gotten you something,

01:06:03.723 --> 01:06:04.956
Miss Leigh.
Oh.

01:06:05.125 --> 01:06:07.625
[Leigh]
This is all so sweet.
[chuckles]

01:06:07.794 --> 01:06:09.289
I'm sorry about Lindsay.

01:06:09.458 --> 01:06:11.293
I-I thought this might be
hard for her.

01:06:11.462 --> 01:06:13.798
[Jeffrey]
Yeah. No, and, look,
I understand that.

01:06:13.967 --> 01:06:15.327
[Dee]
This one has to go on top.

01:06:15.529 --> 01:06:17.401
[Jeffrey]
Yeah, the top, top part.

01:06:19.201 --> 01:06:21.169
And this one
has to go...

01:06:21.372 --> 01:06:22.840
[Jeffrey] But wait,
where's the light...

01:06:23.042 --> 01:06:25.745
[Dee]
Wait, you got to connect.

01:06:25.914 --> 01:06:26.841
[Jeffrey]
Oh, the click.
[chuckles]

01:06:27.043 --> 01:06:28.309
I love the click.

01:06:28.478 --> 01:06:29.512
And this one
has to go on that.
[Leigh] Dee?

01:06:29.681 --> 01:06:30.814
Yeah.

01:06:30.982 --> 01:06:32.620
It's 11:00.
Past 11:00.

01:06:32.789 --> 01:06:34.117
Oh, come on,
let us finish this. Please?

01:06:34.286 --> 01:06:35.546
Please?
She's, like, the best builder.

01:06:35.748 --> 01:06:37.018
We're like 20 pieces away
from the end.

01:06:37.186 --> 01:06:38.382
[Dee]
Yeah, please, Mom.

01:06:38.584 --> 01:06:40.327
So close.
Another time, okay?

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:41.524
[Jeffrey]
Okay.

01:06:42.588 --> 01:06:43.989
I had the best time
with you.

01:06:44.158 --> 01:06:45.165
Okay?
Yeah.

01:06:45.334 --> 01:06:47.194
[grunts]

01:06:47.396 --> 01:06:49.170
[Jeffrey]
<i> Can I see you again?</i>

01:06:49.339 --> 01:06:50.534
I'd like that.

01:06:50.736 --> 01:06:52.634
Yeah?
Yeah.

01:06:52.803 --> 01:06:55.837
So, if it's late,
I'll just come and, like,
tap on your window?

01:06:56.006 --> 01:06:57.642
Oh.
[snickers]

01:06:57.811 --> 01:06:58.976
I don't know if I'm a...

01:06:59.145 --> 01:07:00.840
"tap on the window"
kind of girl, John.

01:07:01.008 --> 01:07:02.708
No?

01:07:02.877 --> 01:07:05.977
All right, how about I just
knock on the front door?

01:07:06.146 --> 01:07:07.517
Okay.

01:07:08.549 --> 01:07:11.554
[piano playing
"I'll be Home"]

01:07:19.769 --> 01:07:22.895
[Pastor Ron]
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:07:25.772 --> 01:07:28.703
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:34.742
♪<i> When your nights</i>
<i> are troubled</i> ♪

01:07:36.411 --> 01:07:39.087
♪<i> And you're all alone</i> ♪

01:07:42.191 --> 01:07:45.222
[choir] ♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪
♪<i> When you're feeling down</i> ♪

01:07:45.390 --> 01:07:50.429
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪
♪<i> You need some sympathy</i> ♪

01:07:50.631 --> 01:07:53.700
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪

01:07:53.869 --> 01:07:55.935
♪<i> There's no one else around</i> ♪

01:07:56.137 --> 01:08:01.275
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪
♪<i> To keep you company</i> ♪

01:08:01.477 --> 01:08:03.705
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪

01:08:04.881 --> 01:08:07.745
♪<i> Ah</i> ♪
♪<i> Remember, baby</i> ♪

01:08:07.914 --> 01:08:09.476
♪<i> You can always</i> ♪

01:08:09.678 --> 01:08:13.981
♪<i> Count on me</i> ♪
♪<i> Count on me</i> ♪

01:08:14.183 --> 01:08:16.790
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:08:16.992 --> 01:08:22.691
♪<i> I'll be home</i>
<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:08:26.866 --> 01:08:29.368
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:08:32.542 --> 01:08:35.440
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:08:38.705 --> 01:08:41.413
♪<i> Wherever you may wander</i> ♪

01:08:44.314 --> 01:08:48.156
♪<i> Wherever you may roam</i> ♪

01:08:49.386 --> 01:08:51.951
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪
♪<i> You come back</i> ♪

01:08:53.458 --> 01:08:57.529
♪<i> I'll be waiting here</i>
<i> for you</i> ♪

01:08:57.731 --> 01:09:00.459
♪<i> Ooh</i> ♪

01:09:00.627 --> 01:09:02.700
♪<i> Ah</i> ♪
♪<i> I'll be here</i> ♪

01:09:02.903 --> 01:09:05.964
♪<i> To comfort you</i> ♪

01:09:06.133 --> 01:09:10.008
♪<i> And see you through</i> ♪
♪<i> And see you through</i> ♪

01:09:10.210 --> 01:09:15.510
♪<i> I'll be home</i>
<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:09:15.713 --> 01:09:17.912
[Leigh] Goodbye, Halloween.
♪<i> I'll be home</i> ♪

01:09:18.081 --> 01:09:19.485
<i> Turkey time.</i>

01:09:19.654 --> 01:09:21.185
[song fades]

01:09:21.387 --> 01:09:22.948
[Leigh]
<i>Don't hit the light.</i>
[Otis]<i> I won't.</i>

01:09:23.117 --> 01:09:25.352
Yeah, maybe next year
we should get
an inflatable Otis.

01:09:25.554 --> 01:09:26.794
[Otis mutters]
[clicks tongue]

01:09:26.963 --> 01:09:29.687
Hey. I-I'm not
stepping in this time.

01:09:29.890 --> 01:09:31.691
Okay? You got to do it.
You got to do it.

01:09:31.893 --> 01:09:34.967
You got to punch the bully
in the nose, you know?

01:09:35.136 --> 01:09:37.128
[keyboard clicking]
[knocking on door]

01:09:38.202 --> 01:09:40.204
My man, Otis.
Yeah.

01:09:40.373 --> 01:09:43.510
Yeah. I need to tell you
something, Mitch.

01:09:43.679 --> 01:09:45.006
Whoa, okay.
Yeah.

01:09:45.175 --> 01:09:46.713
I mean-- okay. What?

01:09:46.882 --> 01:09:48.711
Um...
[breathing heavily]

01:09:50.717 --> 01:09:51.978
What?

01:09:52.950 --> 01:09:54.250
Uh...

01:09:54.453 --> 01:09:56.386
[Otis stammering]
[Jeffrey] Please say it.

01:09:56.555 --> 01:09:58.319
<i> No, I'm sorry.</i>
<i> Um, I'm just...</i>
<i> What, what?</i>

01:09:58.488 --> 01:10:00.990
<i> Uh, I was, I was, um...</i>
Say it.

01:10:01.159 --> 01:10:01.924
<i> Otis, come on.</i>
<i> I...</i>

01:10:02.127 --> 01:10:03.325
[Jeffrey] Just say it.

01:10:03.494 --> 01:10:05.096
<i> I wanted to tell you I-I...</i>
<i> What?</i>

01:10:05.298 --> 01:10:06.865
<i>I sweeped up the stockroom</i>
<i>like you said.</i>

01:10:07.034 --> 01:10:08.401
<i> Okay, is that it?</i>
<i> Yeah.</i>

01:10:08.603 --> 01:10:10.403
No. No.

01:10:12.509 --> 01:10:16.409
[Jeffrey]
<i> My mom used to tell me</i>
<i> be careful what you touch.</i>

01:10:17.942 --> 01:10:21.582
<i> She said that moving one grain</i>
<i> of sand changes everything</i>

01:10:21.784 --> 01:10:24.316
<i> in the whole universe.</i>

01:10:24.485 --> 01:10:27.385
<i> I think people call it</i>
<i> the butterfly effect.</i>

01:10:27.554 --> 01:10:30.222
<i> That just one butterfly</i>
<i> flapping its wings can</i>

01:10:30.391 --> 01:10:33.151
<i>make a hurricane</i>
<i>on the other side of the world.</i>

01:10:34.695 --> 01:10:37.324
<i> And before we know it, we're</i>
<i>banging into each other's paths</i>

01:10:37.493 --> 01:10:39.294
<i> and changing what happens.</i>

01:10:39.497 --> 01:10:41.192
[Leigh]
Are you sure you want bangs?

01:10:41.361 --> 01:10:42.536
Sure.

01:10:42.705 --> 01:10:43.571
It's a big change.

01:10:43.740 --> 01:10:45.038
Thing is about bangs,

01:10:45.207 --> 01:10:46.566
there's only about
one in a thousand people

01:10:46.735 --> 01:10:48.241
that actually look good
with bangs,

01:10:48.410 --> 01:10:51.072
but good news is I think that
you might be one of them.

01:10:51.241 --> 01:10:52.445
[laughs softly]

01:10:52.614 --> 01:10:54.215
Oh, God.

01:10:54.384 --> 01:10:57.115
[Jeffrey]
<i>No one notices the butterfly</i>
<i>flapping its wings</i>

01:10:57.284 --> 01:11:00.545
<i> until everyone</i>
<i> feels the storm.</i>

01:11:00.714 --> 01:11:03.753
<i> I knew a storm was coming.</i>

01:11:05.019 --> 01:11:06.961
<i> I knew if I stayed</i>
<i> in one place too long,</i>

01:11:07.130 --> 01:11:09.264
<i> eventually someone</i>
<i> would recognize me.</i>

01:11:10.261 --> 01:11:11.794
<i> I knew I had to leave.</i>

01:11:12.826 --> 01:11:14.932
<i> I just didn't want</i>
<i> to go alone.</i>

01:11:15.101 --> 01:11:17.732
[Jeffrey chuckles]
<i> You think you could</i>
<i> ever just move somewhere else?</i>

01:11:17.901 --> 01:11:20.640
Like a beach or something?
Start over in a new place?

01:11:20.842 --> 01:11:21.942
I don't know, John.

01:11:22.111 --> 01:11:23.402
I-I need to come back here,
you know?

01:11:23.571 --> 01:11:25.304
We could take the girls.

01:11:25.506 --> 01:11:26.810
Just pack up and go.

01:11:27.012 --> 01:11:29.616
Mm. That's...

01:11:29.785 --> 01:11:31.882
No, I can't do that.

01:11:32.051 --> 01:11:33.915
I can't do that.

01:11:36.287 --> 01:11:38.392
My life is here,
John.

01:11:41.254 --> 01:11:43.996
["Don't Speak" by No Doubt
playing over headphones]

01:11:44.165 --> 01:11:47.459
[Mitch]
♪<i> You're letting go</i> ♪

01:11:47.628 --> 01:11:49.430
♪<i> And if it's real</i> ♪

01:11:49.599 --> 01:11:52.498
♪<i> Well, I don't want to know</i> ♪

01:11:52.667 --> 01:11:54.169
[Mitch grunting rhythmically]

01:11:54.338 --> 01:11:55.670
♪<i> Don't speak...</i> ♪

01:11:55.838 --> 01:11:59.474
[water running]
[Mitch singing in distance]

01:11:59.643 --> 01:12:01.707
♪<i> Stop explaining</i> ♪
[water stops]

01:12:01.909 --> 01:12:05.716
♪<i> Don't tell me</i>
<i>'Cause it hurts</i> ♪

01:12:06.756 --> 01:12:08.450
♪<i> Don't speak</i> ♪

01:12:08.619 --> 01:12:11.458
♪<i> I know what you're...</i> ♪
[grunts]

01:12:12.490 --> 01:12:14.359
♪<i> I don't need your reasons</i> ♪

01:12:14.562 --> 01:12:17.596
[muffled]
♪<i> Don't tell me</i>
<i> 'Cause it hurts</i> ♪

01:12:18.661 --> 01:12:19.666
[song continues
over headphones]

01:12:19.835 --> 01:12:22.869
♪<i> Our memories</i> ♪

01:12:23.071 --> 01:12:25.270
♪<i> They can be inviting</i> ♪

01:12:25.439 --> 01:12:28.707
♪<i> But some</i>
<i> Erotically enticing</i> ♪

01:12:28.910 --> 01:12:31.975
♪<i> Writing</i> ♪

01:12:32.144 --> 01:12:35.013
♪<i> As we die</i> ♪

01:12:35.181 --> 01:12:38.377
♪<i> Both you and I...</i> ♪

01:12:38.579 --> 01:12:40.179
[singing fades]

01:12:50.394 --> 01:12:52.065
♪<i> Stop explaining</i> ♪

01:12:52.234 --> 01:12:55.396
♪<i> Don't tell me</i>
<i>'Cause it hurts</i> ♪

01:12:55.564 --> 01:12:57.702
♪<i> No, no, no, no, no</i> ♪

01:12:59.205 --> 01:13:00.540
[gasps] What the fuck?

01:13:00.709 --> 01:13:01.873
[yells]

01:13:02.042 --> 01:13:03.602
What? Oh, my God!

01:13:03.804 --> 01:13:05.945
[Jeffrey yelling]
Oh, my God!

01:13:06.147 --> 01:13:08.680
[Jeffrey continues yelling]

01:13:10.646 --> 01:13:12.618
[door opens]
[alarm wailing]

01:13:15.218 --> 01:13:17.249
[grunting]

01:13:19.695 --> 01:13:21.927
[panting]

01:13:22.129 --> 01:13:24.157
[alarm continues wailing]

01:13:25.624 --> 01:13:27.666
[grunting]

01:13:39.707 --> 01:13:41.782
[clattering]
[grunts]

01:13:41.984 --> 01:13:43.946
[alarm continues wailing]

01:13:47.924 --> 01:13:49.755
[sirens wailing outside]

01:13:49.924 --> 01:13:51.988
[siren whoops]

01:13:52.191 --> 01:13:53.960
[sirens wailing]

01:13:54.128 --> 01:13:56.090
[alarm continues wailing]

01:14:07.810 --> 01:14:09.272
[Mitch over headphones]
<i> Oh, my God,</i>
<i> there's a lot of you.</i>

01:14:09.441 --> 01:14:11.272
<i> He's-he's big. He's naked!</i>

01:14:11.441 --> 01:14:12.606
<i> He came at me.</i>

01:14:12.775 --> 01:14:13.738
[officer]
<i> Sir, is he still here?</i>

01:14:13.906 --> 01:14:15.249
[Mitch]
<i> I don't know.</i>

01:14:15.418 --> 01:14:17.216
<i>I heard the-the outer...</i>
<i>the alarm door went off.</i>

01:14:17.385 --> 01:14:18.879
[officer]
<i>So he may have gone outside?</i>

01:14:19.048 --> 01:14:20.652
[Mitch]<i> Uh, yes.</i>
[officer]
Charlotte Police!

01:14:20.854 --> 01:14:23.155
[officer 2] Charlotte Police!
[officer]
Charlotte Police!

01:14:23.358 --> 01:14:25.126
Police department!
Police department!

01:14:25.295 --> 01:14:27.995
[indistinct shouting]
Police department!

01:14:28.198 --> 01:14:30.564
Police department!
Police department!

01:14:33.430 --> 01:14:34.563
[siren whooping]

01:14:34.732 --> 01:14:36.302
[officer]
<i> The alarm was going off.</i>

01:14:36.471 --> 01:14:39.064
<i>When we came back here,</i>
<i>the door was ajar,</i>

01:14:39.232 --> 01:14:41.573
<i> so we really believe</i>
<i>he went out this way.</i>

01:14:41.742 --> 01:14:43.610
[Mitch]<i> We could watch</i>
<i>the whole thing, Officer,</i>

01:14:43.778 --> 01:14:46.408
<i>'cause I know how to... press</i>
<i> "play" on this thing, so...</i>

01:14:46.577 --> 01:14:47.841
[Scheimreif]<i> Mitch?</i>
<i> Yeah?</i>

01:14:48.043 --> 01:14:49.512
<i>The good news is</i>
<i>you have surveillance cameras</i>

01:14:49.681 --> 01:14:51.446
<i>all over the store.</i>
[Mitch]<i> Yes. Yes.</i>

01:14:51.614 --> 01:14:53.218
[Scheimreif]
<i>Bad news...</i>

01:14:53.420 --> 01:14:55.622
<i>is none of them</i>
<i>were recording.</i>

01:14:56.619 --> 01:14:58.658
You need
to fix that.

01:15:00.990 --> 01:15:04.362
Now, besides
the naked guy,
have you noticed

01:15:04.531 --> 01:15:07.535
anything strange
happening around here?

01:15:09.772 --> 01:15:11.737
Uh, uh...

01:15:13.434 --> 01:15:17.877
Uh, well, we're-we're missing
a lot of gaming inventory.

01:15:18.046 --> 01:15:19.470
[mutters softly]

01:15:20.740 --> 01:15:22.308
What's a lot?

01:15:23.745 --> 01:15:25.685
A substantial amount.

01:15:27.485 --> 01:15:30.850
[Scheimreif]<i> You're gonna</i>
<i> have to get some real security</i>
<i> in here, Mitch.</i>

01:15:31.019 --> 01:15:32.785
[reporter]
<i>Workers at this Toys "R" Us</i>

01:15:32.954 --> 01:15:34.788
<i>are prepping</i>
<i>for the holiday rush,</i>

01:15:34.957 --> 01:15:36.859
<i>but store manager</i>
<i>Mitch Haggin says</i>

01:15:37.028 --> 01:15:40.298
<i> he did not expect to see</i>
<i>what he saw this morning:</i>

01:15:40.466 --> 01:15:43.732
<i>a strong, very tall, naked man.</i>

01:15:43.934 --> 01:15:46.472
[Mitch over TV]
<i>Uh, a-a naked guy ran at me.</i>

01:15:46.640 --> 01:15:48.404
<i>I think he was gonna kill me,</i>
<i>and I ran away,</i>

01:15:48.606 --> 01:15:49.968
<i>locked myself in my office.</i>

01:15:50.137 --> 01:15:51.277
[reporter]
<i>When I asked if the naked man</i>

01:15:51.479 --> 01:15:53.007
<i> would scare off</i>
<i>holiday shoppers,</i>

01:15:53.176 --> 01:15:56.408
<i>Mr. Haggin said he was hiring</i>
<i>round-the-clock security.</i>

01:15:56.577 --> 01:15:59.216
<i> We have a really good security</i>
<i> system here now, for sure.</i>

01:15:59.385 --> 01:16:00.585
<i>Families can feel safe.</i>

01:16:00.753 --> 01:16:02.389
<i> This is a safe place</i>
<i>to come for Christmas.</i>

01:16:02.558 --> 01:16:03.889
[Leigh]
I think it looks great.
[TV clicks off]

01:16:04.058 --> 01:16:05.087
Hi.
Hi.

01:16:05.255 --> 01:16:06.686
Hi.

01:16:06.854 --> 01:16:08.591
We're almost
ready to go.

01:16:08.760 --> 01:16:10.425
[Pastor Ron]
<i>Lord, we want to thank you</i>

01:16:10.594 --> 01:16:12.466
for this wonderful food,

01:16:12.668 --> 01:16:15.527
and we want to thank you
for the gift of family. Amen.

01:16:15.696 --> 01:16:17.403
[all]
Amen.

01:16:17.572 --> 01:16:19.697
Happy Thanksgiving.
Happy Thanksgiving.

01:16:19.866 --> 01:16:20.933
Happy Thanksgiving.

01:16:21.102 --> 01:16:22.504
Happy Thanksgiving.
[happy chatter]

01:16:22.672 --> 01:16:24.270
[Eileen]
So, Leigh.
Yes?

01:16:24.472 --> 01:16:28.743
Why don't you tell us all
that story about the naked man.

01:16:28.912 --> 01:16:30.908
[chuckles]
Oh, it-it's nothing, y'all.

01:16:31.076 --> 01:16:32.682
It... it was cold outside,

01:16:32.851 --> 01:16:35.013
and a homeless man
needed to take a shower.

01:16:35.182 --> 01:16:37.553
Yeah, but what if
he's also a killer?

01:16:37.722 --> 01:16:39.519
He's...
Stop being overdramatic.

01:16:39.688 --> 01:16:40.854
He's not a killer.

01:16:41.023 --> 01:16:42.063
[chuckles]
Your mom's totally right.

01:16:42.231 --> 01:16:43.723
He's definitely not
a killer.

01:16:43.892 --> 01:16:45.466
You don't know that,
John.

01:16:45.668 --> 01:16:47.460
Well, if he was a killer,
he'd have killed him, right?

01:16:47.663 --> 01:16:50.803
Uh, the paper said today
that there was $10,000
in video games stolen.

01:16:51.004 --> 01:16:52.572
Mm.

01:16:52.741 --> 01:16:53.833
[Randy] I don't know
if that's a coincidence or not.

01:16:54.035 --> 01:16:55.142
[Eileen]
That is a lot of money.

01:16:55.311 --> 01:16:56.273
[Lindsay]
Well, I don't know, Mom.

01:16:56.442 --> 01:16:57.572
Maybe you should quit.

01:16:57.741 --> 01:16:59.070
You have
a master's degree,

01:16:59.239 --> 01:17:01.972
and I don't think
it's worth the risk.

01:17:02.141 --> 01:17:04.076
It seems scary
over there.

01:17:04.245 --> 01:17:06.681
I mean, that's not
the worst idea,
I guess.

01:17:06.884 --> 01:17:08.479
I like my job.
[Randy] Wait. Hold up.

01:17:08.648 --> 01:17:10.682
Earlier, you just made it seem
like it wasn't dangerous.

01:17:10.884 --> 01:17:16.660
So, if it's not dangerous,
then-then why does
she have to quit so suddenly?

01:17:16.829 --> 01:17:18.528
[Pastor Ron] Yeah.
I don't know.
I'm sorry.

01:17:18.731 --> 01:17:20.959
Uh, did I, did I say
she had to quit?

01:17:21.127 --> 01:17:22.535
I don't think I did,
actually.

01:17:22.738 --> 01:17:24.237
I think I was just agreeing
with Lindsay down here.

01:17:24.406 --> 01:17:26.172
I was just saying here
that Lindsay

01:17:26.374 --> 01:17:27.666
actually has
a great idea.

01:17:27.869 --> 01:17:29.740
If she wants to quit,

01:17:29.908 --> 01:17:31.839
then she would
have more time
with her girls.

01:17:32.041 --> 01:17:33.280
Yeah.
[Pastor Ron]
Now, everybody,

01:17:33.449 --> 01:17:35.976
let's not get too serious,
because, uh...

01:17:36.145 --> 01:17:39.352
[laughing] I just think
it's kind of funny.

01:17:39.555 --> 01:17:42.686
I imagine the guy,
he's just going to work,

01:17:42.888 --> 01:17:45.184
just a normal day,
and then he sees a naked guy

01:17:45.386 --> 01:17:47.351
running around
inside his toy store.
[laughter]

01:17:47.554 --> 01:17:49.191
[Kami] Makes me want
to get a job there,
actually.

01:17:49.393 --> 01:17:50.689
[laughter]

01:17:50.891 --> 01:17:52.928
Oh, Kami, bless you.

01:17:53.097 --> 01:17:55.301
Yeah, I just think
it's really funny,
that's all.

01:17:55.469 --> 01:17:57.036
I don't think
it's funny, Ron.

01:17:57.205 --> 01:17:58.502
I-I think it's sad.

01:17:58.670 --> 01:18:00.197
I mean,
someone's so desperate

01:18:00.366 --> 01:18:03.034
they had to bathe
in a toy store sink,

01:18:03.203 --> 01:18:05.312
while we eat
and laugh about it?

01:18:05.481 --> 01:18:09.575
I mean, maybe we aren't
Good Samaritans.

01:18:09.777 --> 01:18:11.310
[Eileen]
Mm.

01:18:11.479 --> 01:18:14.020
[Lindsay] Maybe you aren't
making the best decisions.

01:18:14.189 --> 01:18:15.754
Excuse me, ma'am?

01:18:15.956 --> 01:18:18.515
Choosing to work there
while Dee and I
are home alone,

01:18:18.684 --> 01:18:20.523
waiting for someone
to pick us up
to take us places?

01:18:20.691 --> 01:18:22.487
Like, we...
Whoa, whoa.

01:18:22.656 --> 01:18:24.924
If we're being honest,
you're old enough
to drive yourself.

01:18:25.126 --> 01:18:26.266
[Lindsay]
I don't have a license.

01:18:26.469 --> 01:18:28.392
I told you
I would teach you.
Okay?

01:18:28.594 --> 01:18:30.968
[Lindsay] I can't even
sit in the car with you.

01:18:31.137 --> 01:18:33.405
And now that Dad's not here,
you bring around this weirdo,

01:18:33.608 --> 01:18:35.974
and we're supposed
to just accept it?

01:18:36.972 --> 01:18:38.675
I-I hope the sex
is worth it.

01:18:38.844 --> 01:18:41.408
[gasps]
[Pastor Ron]
Hey, hey, hey.

01:18:42.448 --> 01:18:43.883
[Leigh]
Lin...

01:18:48.280 --> 01:18:49.581
[Leigh clears throat
softly]

01:18:50.652 --> 01:18:52.254
Sorry.

01:18:54.527 --> 01:18:55.892
[chair scrapes on floor]

01:18:56.061 --> 01:18:57.260
[Kami whispers]
Our church.
[Pastor Ron] Yeah.

01:18:57.463 --> 01:18:59.593
[quiet chatter]

01:18:59.762 --> 01:19:01.628
[phone ringing]

01:19:01.830 --> 01:19:03.027
[Pastor Ron]
Wow.

01:19:03.195 --> 01:19:05.201
[phone continues ringing]

01:19:10.172 --> 01:19:11.874
Hello?
[Jeffrey over phone]<i> Uh, hi.</i>

01:19:12.043 --> 01:19:13.378
[whispering]
Um, this is Cousin Oliver.

01:19:13.547 --> 01:19:14.643
I was just calling
for Steve.

01:19:14.845 --> 01:19:16.076
<i> It's 7:00 in the morning.</i>

01:19:16.245 --> 01:19:17.781
[Jeffrey]
Uh, it's also December 1st,

01:19:17.950 --> 01:19:19.815
and we had a conversation
a few months back

01:19:20.017 --> 01:19:21.588
that I should call back
on December 1st.

01:19:21.757 --> 01:19:23.281
<i> Yeah, you just call back.</i>
<i> He's sleeping.</i>

01:19:23.450 --> 01:19:25.590
Okay, well, can you
just wake him up for me?

01:19:25.759 --> 01:19:27.051
Um, just tell him
it's Cousin Oliver.

01:19:27.219 --> 01:19:28.159
All right?
It's urgent.

01:19:28.362 --> 01:19:29.891
Baby.
Mm. Mm.

01:19:30.060 --> 01:19:31.363
It's your cousin.
It's Cousin Oliver.

01:19:31.532 --> 01:19:33.795
[groans] Tell him I'm asleep.

01:19:33.997 --> 01:19:36.302
[muttering]
Motherfucker. Goddamn.

01:19:36.504 --> 01:19:37.731
He says...
We can do it Sunday.

01:19:37.900 --> 01:19:39.362
...he's asleep and that

01:19:39.531 --> 01:19:41.103
<i> you should come</i>
<i> see him next Sunday.</i>

01:19:41.272 --> 01:19:43.873
Next Sunday.
Okay, great. Is he
still in Fayetteville?

01:19:44.042 --> 01:19:47.047
<i> No. No.</i>
<i> It's the Twin Pines Motel.</i>

01:19:47.216 --> 01:19:48.410
Twin Pines. Okay.

01:19:48.579 --> 01:19:49.878
<i> Room 204.</i>

01:19:50.047 --> 01:19:51.550
204. I got it.
[Steve]<i> And don't be</i>

01:19:51.719 --> 01:19:53.214
a fucking dumbass
and take the bus.

01:19:53.383 --> 01:19:54.949
He says don't be a fucking
dumbass and take the bus.

01:19:55.118 --> 01:19:56.713
<i> He wants to know</i>
<i>if you got a car.</i>

01:19:56.882 --> 01:19:59.426
[Jeffrey] Yep. Tell the sarge,
uh, I'll take care of that

01:19:59.595 --> 01:20:02.127
and I'll see him on Sunday
as scheduled.

01:20:02.296 --> 01:20:03.261
[phone beeps]

01:20:03.430 --> 01:20:04.624
[dishes clatter]

01:20:04.793 --> 01:20:06.196
H-Hi. Morning.

01:20:08.066 --> 01:20:10.431
You didn't tell me
you had to take a trip.

01:20:12.101 --> 01:20:14.668
You weren't supposed
to hear that.

01:20:14.837 --> 01:20:16.837
[laughs]
Okay.

01:20:17.006 --> 01:20:18.335
Look, it's not a big deal.

01:20:18.504 --> 01:20:20.047
I just have to go
and just check in.

01:20:20.249 --> 01:20:21.882
That's all.
Okay.

01:20:23.844 --> 01:20:25.283
Mwah.

01:20:25.452 --> 01:20:27.118
Morning, Lindsay.

01:20:28.690 --> 01:20:30.781
Good morning, Leigh.
Good morning, Dee.

01:20:31.924 --> 01:20:34.021
Everybody want to say
"good morning"?

01:20:34.223 --> 01:20:36.655
[Dee] Morning, John.
[Jeffrey chuckles]

01:20:42.331 --> 01:20:45.664
All right, who wants
to apologize first, hmm?

01:20:47.967 --> 01:20:49.209
No? You?

01:20:49.411 --> 01:20:50.940
Come on, guys.
[stammers]

01:20:51.109 --> 01:20:53.312
Nobody has anything
to say to each other?

01:20:53.481 --> 01:20:55.305
Look, families fight.

01:20:55.474 --> 01:20:57.951
That's fine,
but they also make up.

01:20:59.286 --> 01:21:00.613
Come on.

01:21:02.353 --> 01:21:04.688
I'm sorry for the way
I've been acting, Lindsay.

01:21:04.857 --> 01:21:06.751
[knocks on counter]
Great work.

01:21:12.067 --> 01:21:15.034
I shouldn't have said
the thing about sex
in front of Dee.

01:21:16.369 --> 01:21:17.696
Mm. Yeah.

01:21:17.865 --> 01:21:19.029
And...

01:21:19.198 --> 01:21:21.403
And? You got it.

01:21:22.401 --> 01:21:24.375
And I need a ride
to Doug's.

01:21:24.544 --> 01:21:25.775
Nope. That wasn't...

01:21:25.977 --> 01:21:27.607
You aren't getting
a ride anywhere.

01:21:27.809 --> 01:21:30.678
Do you have any idea
how much you embarrassed me
last night?

01:21:30.847 --> 01:21:32.384
I embarrassed you?

01:21:32.553 --> 01:21:34.052
John, will you drive me?

01:21:34.221 --> 01:21:37.922
You do not get to abuse him
and then ask him for favors.

01:21:38.124 --> 01:21:39.551
[Jeffrey] It's okay.
I-I don't mind driving her.

01:21:39.720 --> 01:21:41.718
No, stay out of this, John.
See, he doesn't mind.

01:21:41.887 --> 01:21:44.856
If she wants to go somewhere,
she can learn to drive.

01:21:45.025 --> 01:21:48.494
I'm not driving in that car
with that stick shift
with you ever.

01:21:48.663 --> 01:21:50.934
Well, then I guess
you'll never go anywhere again!

01:21:51.136 --> 01:21:52.838
[Jeffrey]
Okay, time-out. Time-out.
Ever!

01:21:53.007 --> 01:21:55.170
I'm sorry, can I ask my mom
to drive me places

01:21:55.338 --> 01:21:57.100
'cause she's my mother?
[Jeffrey] Okay, stop.

01:21:57.303 --> 01:21:58.712
I have an idea, okay?

01:21:58.880 --> 01:22:00.939
I have an idea. Hear me out.
It's a great idea.

01:22:01.141 --> 01:22:03.016
We need a beater.

01:22:04.080 --> 01:22:06.445
What even is a beater,
John?

01:22:06.614 --> 01:22:09.649
["Little Drummer Boy"
by Jim Nabors playing]

01:22:10.625 --> 01:22:13.884
♪<i> Come, they told me</i> ♪

01:22:14.053 --> 01:22:15.960
♪<i> Pa, rum, pum, pum, pum...</i> ♪
[Jeffrey speaks indistinctly]

01:22:16.129 --> 01:22:18.229
[salesman] That's a nice ride
right there, huh?

01:22:19.261 --> 01:22:21.625
Classic 1999
with very low mileage.

01:22:21.793 --> 01:22:23.302
[Jeffrey] Yeah?
[salesman]
Great color, too.

01:22:23.471 --> 01:22:24.636
Awesome family car.

01:22:24.804 --> 01:22:26.067
[Jeffrey]
It's automatic.

01:22:26.236 --> 01:22:28.465
[salesman]
It is automatic.
Great price.

01:22:28.634 --> 01:22:30.775
You guys
want to try it out?
Yeah.

01:22:30.944 --> 01:22:34.140
Got the keys right here.
Look at that.

01:22:34.309 --> 01:22:36.146
[sighs]
It's nice seats, right?

01:22:36.348 --> 01:22:38.585
You know, modern cars
just don't have the same feel.

01:22:38.754 --> 01:22:40.385
This is kind of like
the golden era.

01:22:40.554 --> 01:22:42.785
The '90s. [sighs]

01:22:42.954 --> 01:22:46.658
You know, just... [stammers]
They don't make modern cars
like this anymore, you know?

01:22:46.860 --> 01:22:48.320
Yeah.
These-these are like sofas.

01:22:48.522 --> 01:22:50.289
You guys buckled up?
[Leigh] Yeah, yeah.

01:22:50.458 --> 01:22:52.289
Any cops around here ever?
Oh, no, no.

01:22:52.458 --> 01:22:53.830
Nobody's gonna stop you here.

01:22:54.033 --> 01:22:55.095
Just gonna push it
just a little bit.

01:22:55.264 --> 01:22:57.503
[engine revving]
[tires squealing]

01:22:57.705 --> 01:22:59.402
[salesman chuckles]
Okay.

01:23:01.037 --> 01:23:02.508
Okay.
[girls laugh]

01:23:02.710 --> 01:23:04.742
[chuckles]
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

01:23:04.911 --> 01:23:06.577
It's got some horsepower.
Okay.

01:23:06.746 --> 01:23:08.515
All right, all right.

01:23:08.684 --> 01:23:09.846
Got a nice V-6...
[engine revving]

01:23:10.014 --> 01:23:12.113
Okay. Okay.
[yells nervously]

01:23:12.282 --> 01:23:13.648
[tires squealing]
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

01:23:13.817 --> 01:23:14.981
Hey, sir! Sir!

01:23:15.150 --> 01:23:16.457
Watch out!
Here we go.

01:23:16.625 --> 01:23:18.183
Oh. Oh! Oh!
[tires squealing]

